helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	id	You can set the locale used for controlling the formatting numbers, dates and currencies in $[officename] Basic in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>. In Basic format codes, the decimal point (\<emph\>.\</emph\>) is always used as \<emph\>placeholder\</emph\> for the decimal separator defined in your locale and will be replaced by the corresponding character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	id	Hal yang sama juga terjadi pada pengaturan lokal untuk tanggal, waktu, dan format mata uang. Kode format Basic akan diinterpretasi dan ditampilkan menurut pengaturan lokal Anda.				20181231 09:50:43
