helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	id	Returns the sine of an angle. The angle is specified in radians. The result lies between -1 and 1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	id	Using the angle Alpha, the Sin Function returns the ratio of the length of the opposite side of an angle to the length of the hypotenuse in a right-angled triangle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	id	Sin(Alpha) = side opposite the angle/hypotenuse				20181231 09:50:43
