helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	id	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that you want to calculate the natural logarithm for.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	id	The natural logarithm is the logarithm to the base e. Base e is a constant with an approximate value of 2.718282...				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	id	You can calculate logarithms to any base (n) for any number (x) by dividing the natural logarithm of x by the natural logarithm of n, as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	id	Log n(x) = Log(x) / Log(n)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155131				0	id	Contoh:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152463				0	id	Sub ExampleLogExp				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	id	Dim a as Double				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	id	Dim const b1=12.345e12				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	id	Dim const b2=1.345e34				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	id	a=Exp( Log(b1)+Log(b2) )				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	id	MsgBox "" & a & chr(13) & (b1*b2) ,0,"Perkalian oleh fungsi logaritma"				20181231 09:50:43
