helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>procedures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;passing to procedures and functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>parameters;for procedures and functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>parameters;passing by reference or value\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;scope\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scope of variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>GLOBAL variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PUBLIC variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PRIVATE variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>functions;return value type\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>return value type of functions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	id	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/01020300.xhp\"\>Menggunakan Prosedur dan Fungsi\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	id	Berikut ini dijelaskan penggunaan-penggunaan dasar untuk prosedur dan fungsi di dalam $[officename] Basic.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151215				0	id	When you create a new module, $[officename] Basic automatically inserts a SUB called "Main". This default name has nothing to do with the order or the starting point of a $[officename] Basic project. You can also safely rename this SUB.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id314756320				0	id	Some restrictions apply for the names of your public variables, subs, and functions. You must not use the same name as one of the modules of the same library.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124				0	id	Procedures (SUBS) and functions (FUNCTIONS) help you maintaining a structured overview by separating a program into logical pieces.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153193				0	id	Satu keuntungan dari prosedur dan fungsi adalah ketika Anda selesai mengembangkan sebuah kode program yang mengandung komponen-komponen tugas di dalamnya, maka kode-kode ini bisa Anda pakai pada proyek yang lain.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153770				0	id	Melewatkan Variabel ke Prosedur (SUB) dan Fungsi (FUNCTION)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	id	Variables can be passed to both procedures and functions. The SUB or FUNCTION must be declared to expect parameters:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	id	SUB NamaSub(\<emph\>Parameter1 As Type, Parameter2 As Type,...\</emph\>)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151114				0	id	Kode program				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	id	END SUB				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	id	SUB dipanggil dengan sintaksis berikut:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	id	NamaSub(Nilai1, Nilai2,...)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	id	The parameters passed to a SUB must fit to those specified in the SUB declaration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147397				0	id	The same process applies to FUNCTIONS. In addition, functions always return a function result. The result of a function is defined by assigning the return value to the function name:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149412				0	id	FUNCTION NamaFungsi(Parameter1 As Type, Parameter2 As Type,...) As Type				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	id	Kode program				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	id	\<emph\>NamaFungsi=Hasil\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	id	End Function				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153839				0	id	FUNCTION dipanggil dengan sintaksis berikut:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146914				0	id	Variabel=NamaFungsi(Parameter1, Parameter2,...)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B3				0	id	You can also use the fully qualified name to call a procedure or function:\<br/\>\<item type=\"literal\"\>Library.Module.Macro()\</item\>\<br/\> For example, to call the Autotext macro from the Gimmicks library, use the following command:\<br/\>\<item type=\"literal\"\>Gimmicks.AutoText.Main()\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156276				0	id	Passing Variables by Value or Reference				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155765				0	id	Parameters can be passed to a SUB or a FUNCTION either by reference or by value. Unless otherwise specified, a parameter is always passed by reference. That means that a SUB or a FUNCTION gets the parameter and can read and modify its value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	id	If you want to pass a parameter by value insert the key word "ByVal" in front of the parameter when you call a SUB or FUNCTION, for example:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	id	Result = Function(Parameter \<emph\>ByVal\</emph\>)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	id	In this case, the original content of the parameter will not be modified by the FUNCTION since it only gets the value and not the parameter itself.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150982				0	id	Scope of Variables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149814				0	id	A variable defined within a SUB or FUNCTION, only remains valid until the procedure is exited. This is known as a "local" variable. In many cases, you need a variable to be valid in all procedures, in every module of all libraries, or after a SUB or FUNCTION is exited.				20181231 09:50:43
