helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155746				0	id	Decimal accuracy				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146096	138			0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DECIMAL_ACCURACY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.\</ahelp\>With numerical and currency fields you can determine the number of digits displayed to the right of the decimal point.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151340				0	id	Nama				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819	10			0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAME\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>On the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> tab page, this option specifies the name for the control field. On the \<emph\>Form Properties \</emph\>tab page, this option specifies the name for the form.\</ahelp\>Each control field and each form has a \<emph\>Name \</emph\>property through which it can be identified. The name will appear in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\> and, using the name, the control field can be referred to from a macro. The default settings already specify a name which is constructed from using the field's label and number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	id	If you work with macros, make sure that the names of the controls are unique.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146325				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>controls; grouping\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>groups;of controls\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>forms; grouping controls\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146325				0	id	The name is also used to group different controls that belong together functionally, such as radio buttons. To do so, give the same name to all members of the group: controls with identical names form a group. Grouped controls can be represented visually by using a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Group Box\"\>Group Box\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149720				0	id	Navigation bar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149918	198			0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATIONBAR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of the table control.\</ahelp\>Specifies whether to display the navigation bar on the lower border of table controls.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158426				0	id	Read-only				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153215	43			0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_READONLY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the control is read-only (Yes) or if it can be edited (No).\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Read-only \</emph\>property can be assigned to all controls in which the user can enter text. If you assign the read-only property to an image field which uses graphics from a database, the user will not be able to insert new graphics into the database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148912				0	id	Border				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637	140			0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BORDER\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Determines if the field's border should be displayed "Without frame", with a "3-D look" or "Flat".\</ahelp\>With control fields that have a frame, you can determine the border display on the form using the \<emph\>Border \</emph\>property. You can select among the "Without frame", "3-D look" or "Flat" options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149266				0	id	Tab order				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147483				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TABINDEX\"\>The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property determines the order in which the controls are focused in the form when you press the Tab key.\</ahelp\> In a form that contains more than one control, the focus moves to the next control when you press the Tab key. You can specify the order in which the focus changes with an index under \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156207				0	id	The \<emph\>Tab order\</emph\> property is not available to \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Hidden Controls\"\>Hidden Controls\</link\>. If you want, you can also set this property for image buttons and image controls, so that you can select these controls with the Tab key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150378				0	id	When creating a form, an index is automatically assigned to the control fields that are added to this form; every control field added is assigned an index increased by 1. If you change the index of a control, the indices of the other controls are updated automatically. Elements that cannot be focused (Tabstop = No) are also assigned a value. However, these controls are skipped when using the Tab key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640				0	id	You can also easily define the indices of the different controls in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>\<emph\>Tab Order\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0509200912114423				0	id	Mouse wheel scroll				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200912114566				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets whether the value changes when the user scrolls a mouse wheel. Never: No change of the value. When focused: (default) The value changes when the control has the focus and the wheel is pointing at the control and gets scrolled. Always: The value changes when the wheel is pointing at the control and gets scrolled, no matter which control has the focus.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154049				0	id	Default status				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150837				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_CHECKED\"\>Specifies whether an option or a check box is selected by default.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149242				0	id	For a reset type button, you can define the status of the control if the reset button is activated by the user.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156266				0	id	For grouped option fields, the status of the group corresponding to the default setting is defined by the \<emph\>Default Status\</emph\> property.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156150				0	id	Default selection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148730	37			0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_SELECT_SEQ\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the list box entry to mark as the default entry.\</ahelp\>Specifies the list box entry to mark as the default entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150028	203			0	id	For a Reset type button, the\<emph\> Default selection\</emph\> entry defines the status of the list box if the reset button is activated by the user.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id919217				0	id	For a List box that contains a value list, you can click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open the \<emph\>Default selection\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id50050				0	id	In the \<emph\>Default selection\</emph\> dialog, select the entries that you want to mark as selected when you open the form that contains the list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150460				0	id	Default value				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EFFECTIVEDEFAULT\"\>Sets the default value for the control field.\</ahelp\> For example, the default value will be entered when a form is opened.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740	199			0	id	For a Reset type button, the\<emph\> Default value entry \</emph\>defines the status of the control if the reset button is activated by the user.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B70				0	id	Default scroll value				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B74				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_SCROLLVALUE\"\>Sets the default value for the scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
