helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150129				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the image resolution. Select the measurement units from the list box.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143534				0	id	More options				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id10				0	id	For JPEG files you can set the color depth and the quality.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id435923952				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the color depth from 8 bit grayscale or 24 bit true color.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id355152952				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the compression and quality for the export. Choose from a low quality with minimal file size, up to a high quality and big file size. A high compression means a low quality, a low compression means a high quality.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id11				0	id	For BMP files you can set the compression and the RLE encoding.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id312346798				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Applies RLE (Run Length Encoding) to the BMP graphics.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id12				0	id	For PBM, PGM, and PPM files you can set the encoding.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id344441				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in binary format. The resulting file is smaller than a text file.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3555783				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in ASCII text format. The resulting file is larger than a binary file.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id13				0	id	For PNG files you can set the compression and the interlaced mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id35674840				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether the graphic is to be saved in interlaced mode.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id14				0	id	For GIF files you can set the transparency and the interlaced mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id31456456938				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to save the background of the picture as transparent. Only objects will be visible in the GIF image. Use the Color Replacer to set the transparent color in the picture.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id15				0	id	For EPS files you can set the preview, the color format, the compression, and the version.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779948				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>You must print an EPS file with a PostScript printer. Other printers will only print the embedded preview.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993155271				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether a preview image is exported in the TIFF format together with the actual PostScript file.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993144740				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether a monochrome preview graphic in EPSI format is exported together with the PostScript file. This format only contains printable characters from the 7-bit ASCII code.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993150935				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Compression is not available at this level. Select the Level 1 option if your PostScript printer does not offer the capabilities of Level 2.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993159201				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the Level 2 option if your output device supports colored bitmaps, palette graphics and compressed graphics.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id319947250				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in color.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id993147088				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Exports the file in grayscale tones.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id399153683				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>LZW compression is the compression of a file into a smaller file using a table-based lookup algorithm.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id319952780				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies that you do not wish to use compression.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
