helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	id	If you selected one of the date formats (DMY), (MDY), or (YMD) and you enter numbers without date delimiters, the numbers are interpreted as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650	76			0	id	Number of characters 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150495				0	id	Date format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212				0	id	6				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153056				0	id	Two characters each are taken for day, month, and year in the selected order.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147352				0	id	8				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	id	Four characters are taken for the year, two each for month and day, in the selected order.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	id	5 atau 7				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	id	As with 6 or 8 characters, but the first part of the sequence has one character less. This will suppress a leading zero for month and day.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	id	If you want to include the leading zero in the data you import, in telephone numbers for example, apply the "Text" format to the column.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149287				0	id	Pratampil				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147377				0	id	Shows how the imported text will look after it is separated into columns. To apply a format to a column when it is imported, click a column and select a \<emph\>Column type\</emph\>. When you select a \<emph\>Column type\</emph\>, the column heading displays the applied format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	id	If you want to use a fixed width to separate the imported data into columns, click in the ruler to set the width boundaries.				20181231 09:50:43
