helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	id	Setting a Predefined Border Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	id	Place the cursor in the paragraph for which you want to define a border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	id	Pilih \<emph\>Format - Paragraf\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	id	Select one of the default border styles in the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	id	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	id	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area. You can only change distances to edges that have a border line defined.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543				0	id	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149237				0	id	Setting a Customized Border Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	id	Pilih \<emph\>Format - Paragraf\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	id	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3148948				0	id	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	id	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	id	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area. You can only change distances to edges that have a border line defined.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_paragraph.xhp	0	help	par_id3151178				0	id	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Merging Versions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>documents; merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions;merging document versions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230				0	id	\<variable id=\"redlining_docmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging Versions\"\>Merging Versions\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	id	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	id	When a document has been edited by more than one person, it is possible to merge the edited copies into the original. The only requirement is that the documents differ only and exclusively in the recorded changes - all other original text must be identical.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425				0	id	Open the original document into which you want to merge all copies.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Merge Document\</emph\>. A file selection dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	id	Select the copy of the document from the dialog. If there have been no subsequent changes to the original document, the copy is merged into the original.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	id	If changes have been made to the original document, an error dialog appears that informs you that the merge is unsuccessful.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	id	After you merge the documents you will see the recorded changes from the copy in the original document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Inserting Data From Spreadsheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154186				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>charts;copying with link to source cell range\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; cell ranges from spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;cell ranges from spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations;inserting spreadsheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;inserting spreadsheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in spreadsheets;copying data to other applications\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154186				0	id	\<variable id=\"copytable2application\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copytable2application.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Data From Spreadsheets\"\>Inserting Data From Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	id	Use the clipboard to copy the contents of a single cell. You can also copy a formula from a cell into the clipboard (for example, from the input line of the formula bar) so that the formula can be inserted into a text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	id	To copy a cell range into a text document, select the cell range in the sheet and then use either the clipboard or drag-and-drop to insert the cells into the text document. You will then find an OLE object in the text document, which you can edit further.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	id	If you drag cells to the normal view of a presentation document, the cells will be inserted there as an OLE object. If you drag cells into the outline view, each cell will form a line of the outline view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538				0	id	When you copy a cell range from $[officename] Calc to the clipboard, the drawing objects, OLE objects and charts within this range are also copied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytable2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	id	If you insert a cell range with an enclosed chart, the chart will keep its link to the source cell range only if you copied the chart and the source cell range together.				20181231 09:50:43
