helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Table Design				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155448				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; creating in design view (manually)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>designing; database tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>properties;fields in databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fields;database tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoValue (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>primary keys;design view\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	id	\<variable id=\"data_tabledefine\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\" name=\"Table Design\"\>Table Design\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	id	This section contains information about how to create a new database table in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05010000.xhp\" name=\"design view\"\>design view\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288				0	id	Open the database file of the database where you want a new table. Click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon. Choose \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\> to create a new table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	id	In the Design view, you can now create the fields for your table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349				0	id	Enter new fields in rows from top to bottom. Click the \<emph\>Field Name\</emph\> cell and enter a field name for each data field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id1595507				0	id	Include a "primary key" data field. Base needs a primary key to be able to edit the table contents. A primary key has unique contents for each data record. For example, insert a numerical field, right-click the first column, and choose \<emph\>Primary Key\</emph\> from the context menu. Set \<emph\>AutoValue\</emph\> to "Yes", so Base can automatically increment the value for each new record.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	id	In the next cell to the right, define the \<emph\>Field Type\</emph\>. When you click in the cell, you can select a field type in the combo box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	id	Each field can only accept data corresponding to the specified field type. For example, it is not possible to enter text in a number field. Memo fields in dBASE III format are references to internally-managed text files which can hold up to 64KB text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	id	You can enter an optional \<emph\>Description\</emph\> for each field. The text of the description will appear as a tip on the column headings in the table view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	id	Field Properties				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	id	Enter properties for each selected data field. Depending on the database type, some input facilities may not be available.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	id	In the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> box, enter the default contents for every new record. This contents can be edited later.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	id	In the \<emph\>Entry required\</emph\> box, specify whether or not the field may remain empty.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	id	For the \<emph\>Length\</emph\> box, a combo box may be shown that provides the available choices.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying areas to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; sheet areas, to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;sheet areas in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	id	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_table.xhp\" name=\"Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\"\>Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	id	Open both the text document and the spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	id	Select the sheet area you want to copy.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	id	Point to the selected area and press the mouse button. Keep the mouse button pressed for a moment, then drag the area into the text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	32			0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible next to each other, first drag the mouse pointer to the destination document button. Continue to hold down the mouse button. The document is displayed, and you can move the mouse pointer within the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	id	Once the cursor is located in the place where you want to insert the sheet area, release the mouse button. The sheet area is inserted as an OLE object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	id	You can select and edit the OLE object at any time.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	id	To edit the OLE object, double-click on it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389				0	id	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Working with Forms				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	bm_id5762199				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>opening;forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>design view;creating forms\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	id	\<variable id=\"data_forms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_forms.xhp\"\>Bekerja dengan Formulir\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	id	Using forms, you can define how to present the data. Open a text document or a spreadsheet and insert the controls such as push buttons and list boxes. In the properties dialogs of the controls, you can define what data the forms should display.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	id	Creating a New Form With the Form Wizard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	id	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can create a new form using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01090000.xhp\"\>Form Wizard\</link\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	id	Open the database file where you want to create the new form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	id	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	id	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Form\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	id	Creating a New Form Manually				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	id	Open the database file where you want to create the new form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	id	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	id	Click \<emph\>Create Form in Design View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	id	A new text document opens. Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\"\>Form Controls\</link\> to insert form controls.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10670				0	id	Click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon to access all forms that were created from within the current database window. In addition, you can use the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> icons to add database form controls to any Writer or Calc document, but these documents will not be listed in the database window. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156426				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>faxes; sending\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes;configuring $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as faxes \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>configuring;fax icon\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156426				0	id	\<variable id=\"fax\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fax.xhp\" name=\"Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\"\>Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	id	To send a fax directly from $[officename], you need a fax modem and a fax driver that allows applications to communicate with the fax modem.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410				0	id	Sending a Fax Through the Print Dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	id	Open the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\> and select the fax driver in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135				0	id	Clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\> opens the dialog for your fax driver, where you can select the fax recipient.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	id	Configuring $[officename] a Fax Icon				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	id	You can configure $[officename] so that a single click on an icon automatically sends the current document as a fax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	id	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040400.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Print\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</link\>\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	id	Select the fax driver from the \<emph\>Fax\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EB				0	id	Click the arrow icon at the end of the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar. In the drop-down menu, choose \<emph\>Customize\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	id	The \<emph\>Toolbar\</emph\>s tab page of the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FA				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Huruf\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	id	Select the "Documents" category, then select the "Send Default Fax" command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	id	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	id	On the \<emph\>Toolbars\</emph\> tab page, click the down arrow button to position the new icon where you want it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	id	Your \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar now has a new icon to send the current document as a fax.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Aksesibilitas dalam %PRODUCTNAME				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>aksesibilitas; fitur %PRODUCTNAME\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150502				0	id	\<variable id=\"accessibility\"\>\<link name=\"Aksesibilitas dalam %PRODUCTNAME\" href=\"text/shared/guide/accessibility.xhp\"\>Aksesibilitas dalam \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3154894				0	id	The following accessibility features are part of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894				0	id	Support of \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"external devices and applications\"\>external devices and applications\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	id	Access to all functions by keyboard. The keys that replace the mouse actions are listed in the \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME Help\" href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Help\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	id	Improved readability of screen contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	id	Zooming of on-screen user interface for menus, icons, and documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3145071				0	id	The user interface is scalable through your \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Window Manager\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>operating system\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> settings. The default font size for dialogs is 12pt, corresponding to a scale of 100%. You can also change the font size for dialogs in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - View\</emph\>. The zoom factor of a document can be changed in \<emph\>View - Zoom\</emph\>, or by double-clicking the zoom factor displayed in the Status Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	id	Please note that accessibility support relies on Java technology for communications with assistive technology tools. This means that the first program startup may take a few seconds longer, because the Java runtime environment has to be started as well.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME - View\" href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010800.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - View\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME - Appearance\" href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - Appearance\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME - Accessibility\" href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> - Accessibility\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
