helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156014				0	id	\<variable id=\"text_color\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/text_color.xhp\" name=\"Mengubah Warna Teks\"\>Mengubah Warna Teks\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	id	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon to activate a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#abreissleiste\" name=\"toolbar\"\>toolbar\</link\> from which you can choose from a range of colors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id3159233\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_color.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159233\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3152781				0	id	Warna Huruf				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id3150503\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fillstyle.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150503\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149795				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>paint can symbol\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795				0	id	The following only applies to \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer: If you click the icon with a short-click while no text is selected, then the mouse pointer changes its appearance and is displayed as a paint can. Use this paint can symbol with the mouse key pressed to drag across a text area. This text area takes the selected color. The function remains active for as long as the icon is pressed, or until you click without dragging, or until you press the Escape key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	id	The following applies to all modules (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, Calc, Draw, Impress): Select the text that is to take another color, then click the color you want on the toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Warna huruf\"\>Warna huruf\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Changing Default Templates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154285				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>modifying, see changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing, see also editing and replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default templates; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;editing and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;templates\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285				0	id	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	id	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	id	Modifying Default Templates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	id	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	id	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	id	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	id	Double-click \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> in the list on the left. You will see the user-defined templates in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>. Select the template you have just saved and open the context menu or open the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947				0	id	Resetting Default Templates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	id	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	id	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	id	Using Custom Templates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	id	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109				0	id	Templates in the Template Folder				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	id	You can save a new template with \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> or by selecting "Template" file type in any Save dialog. Save the template in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\> to be able to access the template from within the \<emph\>File - New - From Templates and Documents\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	id	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	id	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143267				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Office;reassigning document types\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>file associations for Microsoft Office\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;file associations in Setup program\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	id	\<variable id=\"ms_doctypes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ms_doctypes.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types\"\>Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	id	To change the association of Microsoft Office file name extensions to open the files either in $[officename] or in Microsoft Office, using Microsoft Windows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314147				0	id	In Windows Explorer, right-click a file of the type that you want to assign to another application.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314268				0	id	In the context menu, choose "Open with..."				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314245				0	id	In the list of applications, select the program that should open the current type of files. Make sure that "Always use this program" is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314243				0	id	If these steps do not apply to your brand of Microsoft Windows, search your Microsoft Windows Help for instructions how to change the file associations.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	About Digital Signatures				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>certificates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;overview\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>security;digital signatures\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	hd_id2767418				0	id	\<variable id=\"digital_signatures\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp\"\>About Digital Signatures\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	id	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can digitally sign your documents and macros. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	hd_id6564531				0	id	Certificates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10639				0	id	To sign a document digitally, you need a personal key, the certificate. A personal key is stored on your computer as a combination of a private key, which must be kept secret, and a public key, which you add to your documents when you sign them.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066D				0	id	Save and sign the document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	id	When you apply a digital signature to a document, a kind of checksum is computed from the document's content plus your personal key. The checksum and your public key are stored together with the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	id	Open a signed document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	id	When someone later opens the document on any computer with a recent version of %PRODUCTNAME, the program will compute the checksum again and compare it with the stored checksum. If both are the same, the program will signal that you see the original, unchanged document. In addition, the program can show you the public key information from the certificate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	id	You can compare the public key with the public key that is published on the web site of the certificate authority.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	id	Whenever someone changes something in the document, this change breaks the digital signature. After the change, there will be no sign that you see the original document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id2008200911381426				0	id	The result of the signature validation is displayed in the status bar and within the Digital Signature dialog. Several documents and macro signatures can exist inside an ODF document. If there is a problem with one signature, then the validation result of that one signature is assumed for all signatures. That is, if there are ten valid signatures and one invalid signature, then the status bar and the status field in the dialog will flag the signature as invalid.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200911571878				0	id	You can see any of the following icons and messages when you open a signed document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200912504050				0	id	Icon in Status bar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200912504061				0	id	Signature status				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200912504010				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id0821200912421569\" src=\"xmlsecurity/res/certificate_16.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id0821200912421569\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200912504189				0	id	The signature is valid.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id082120091250418				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id0821200912431081\" src=\"xmlsecurity/res/notcertificate_16.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id0821200912431081\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200912504133				0	id	The signature is OK, but the certificates could not be validated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200912504165				0	id	The signature and the certificate are OK, but not all parts of the document are signed. (For documents that were signed with old versions of the software, see note below.)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200912504237				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id0821200912435090\" src=\"xmlsecurity/res/caution_11x16.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1146in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id0821200912435090\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200912504233				0	id	The signature is invalid.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	hd_id0821200910191787				0	id	Signatures and software versions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200910191747				0	id	The signing of contents got changed with OpenOffice.org 3.2 and StarOffice 9.2. Now all contents of the files, except the signature file itself (META-INF/documentsignatures.xml) are signed. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id0821200910191774				0	id	When you sign a document with OpenOffice.org 3.2 or StarOffice 9.2 or a later version, and you open that document in an older version of the software, the signature will be displayed as "invalid". Signatures created with older versions of the software will be marked with "only parts of the documents are signed" when loaded in the newer software.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id2008200911583098				0	id	When you load an ODF document, you might see an icon in the status bar and the status field in the dialog that indicates that the document is only partially signed. This status will appear when the signature and certificate are valid, but they were created with a version of OpenOffice.org before 3.2 or StarOffice before 9.2. In versions of OpenOffice.org before 3.0 or StarOffice before 9.0, the document signature was applied to the main contents, pictures and embedded objects only and some contents, like macros, were not signed. In OpenOffice.org 3.0 and StarOffice 9.0 the document signature was applied to most content, including macros. However, the mimetype and the content of the META-INF folder were not signed. And in OpenOffice.org 3.2 and StarOffice 9.2 all contents, except the signature file itself (META-INF/documentsignatures.xml), are signed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	hd_id9354228				0	id	Security Warnings				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id2372508				0	id	When you receive a signed document, and the software reports that the signature is valid, this does not mean that you can be absolutely sure that the document is the same that the sender has sent. Signing documents with software certificates is not a perfectly secure method. Numerous ways are possible to circumvent the security features.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id7953123				0	id	Example: Think about someone who wants to camouflage his identity to be a sender from your bank. He can easily get a certificate using a false name, then send you any signed e-mail pretending he is working for your bank. You will get that e-mail, and the e-mail or the document within has the "valid signed" icon. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id6195257				0	id	Do not trust the icon. Inspect and verify the certificates.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id8635517				0	id	The validation of a signature is not a legally binding guarantee of any kind.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id6075624				0	id	On Windows operating systems, the Windows features of validating a signature are used. On Solaris and Linux systems, files that are supplied by Thunderbird, Mozilla or Firefox are used. You must ensure that the files that are in use within your system are really the original files that were supplied by the original developers. For malevolent intruders, there are numerous ways to replace original files with other files that they supply.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id6819971				0	id	The messages about validation of a signature that you see in %PRODUCTNAME are the messages that the validation files return. The %PRODUCTNAME software has no way to ensure that the messages reflect the true status of any certificate. The %PRODUCTNAME software only displays the messages that other files that are not under control of %PRODUCTNAME report. There is no legal responsibility of %PRODUCTNAME that the displayed messages reflect the true status of a digital signature.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id3204443				0	id	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/How_to_use_digital_Signatures\"\>English Wiki page on digital signatures\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id486465				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_send.xhp\"\>Applying digital signatures\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id3448591				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_receive.xhp\"\>Opening a document using WebDAV over HTTPS\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145071				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; data source view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data source view; drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;from data source view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;from data source view\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	id	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_beamer\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_beamer.xhp\" name=\"Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View\"\>Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111				0	id	A fast way of copying from a data source into a text or spreadsheet document, or of creating forms based on a data source, is by drag-and-drop.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id3155390\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155390\"\>Mouse pointer copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	id	Copying with Drag-and-Drop				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	id	If you want to reverse a drag-and-drop, position the cursor in your document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	id	It is also possible to copy by drag-and-drop from a document into a data source:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	id	A text table or the selected range of a spreadsheet can be dragged using drag-and-drop to a table container in the data source explorer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	id	Plain text can be copied using drag-and-drop from one document to a data field in the data source view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145421				0	id	Using data in a text document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685				0	id	You can insert a database field in a text document by dragging a field name from the column header of the data source view into the document. This is especially useful when designing form letters. Simply drag the desired fields - home address, form of address, and so on - into your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153105				0	id	To insert a complete record, select the corresponding header and drag it into the document. When you release the mouse button, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Insert database columns\"\>\<emph\>Insert database columns\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can decide whether to use all database fields, and whether to copy the data into the document as text, a table or fields. All currently selected records will be inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230				0	id	Applying data to a table document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864				0	id	You can insert one or more records into the current sheet of a spreadsheet by selecting the rows in the data source view and dragging and dropping them into the spreadsheet. The data is inserted at the place where you release the mouse button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766				0	id	Inserting controls in a text form				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	id	When you create a text form linked to a database, you can generate controls by drag-and-drop from the data source view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	id	When you drag a database column into the text document, you insert a field. If you hold down Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging, a text field is inserted, grouped with an appropriate label field. The text field already contains all the database information that you need for the form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>opening;documents on WebDAV server\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	hd_id4989165				0	id	\<variable id=\"digitalsign_receive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_receive.xhp\"\>Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	id	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can open and save documents that are stored on a WebDAV server, using the secure HTTPS protocol.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	id	You must use the %PRODUCTNAME file dialogs to use WebDAV over HTTPS.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	id	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\>. Ensure that \<emph\>Use %PRODUCTNAME dialogs\</emph\> is enabled. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7424237				0	id	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter the path to the WebDAV folder. For example, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>https://192.168.1.1/webfolder\</item\> to open a secure connection to the WebDAV server at the IP address 192.168.1.1, and to list the contents of the \<item type=\"literal\"\>webfolder\</item\> folder.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	id	The first time you connect to a WebDAV server, you see the "\<emph\>Website Certified by an Unknown Authority\</emph\>" dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	id	You should click the \<emph\>Examine Certificate\</emph\> button and examine the certificate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	id	If you accept the certificate, choose "\<emph\>Accept this certificate temporarily for this session\</emph\>" and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. Now you can open and save files from the WebDAV server without further questions, until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	id	If you do not trust the certificate, click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	id	If you did accept the certificate, you can now select the file name or file names you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	id	If there is a mismatch of the domain name given in the certificate and the domain name you entered in the file dialog, then you see a dialog that allows you to choose from any of the following options:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	id	 \<emph\>View Certificate\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the View Certificate dialog.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	id	 \<emph\>Continue\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you are sure both domains are the same, click the Continue button.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	id	 \<emph\>Cancel Connection\</emph\> - Cancels the connection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	id	If you click \<emph\>Continue\</emph\>, you may see a dialog that asks you to enter your user name and password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your user name to log on to the WebDAV server.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your password.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If you enable \<emph\>Remember password till end of session\</emph\>, your password will be remembered for subsequent WebDAV connections until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3204443				0	id	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/How_to_use_digital_Signatures\"\>English Wiki page on digital signatures\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id2182378				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp\"\>About digital signatures\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
