helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152924				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>sending; AutoAbstract function in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoAbstract function for sending text to presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>outlines; sending to presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; copying by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; copying and pasting text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152924				0	id	\<variable id=\"copytext2application\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copytext2application.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Data From Text Documents\"\>Inserting Data From Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	id	You can insert text into other document types, such as spreadsheets and presentations. Note that there is a difference between whether the text is inserted into a text frame, a spreadsheet cell, or into the outline view of a presentation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	id	If you copy text to the clipboard, you can paste it with or without text attributes. Use the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V to paste.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id3143270\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_paste.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3143270\"\>Ikon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	id	To select the format in which the clipboard contents will be pasted, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>, then select the proper format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	id	If a text document contains headings formatted with the Heading Paragraph Style, choose \<emph\>File - Send - Outline to Presentation\</emph\>. A new presentation document is created, which contains the headings as an outline.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3145316				0	id	If you want to transfer each heading together with its accompanying paragraphs, select the \<emph\>File - Send - AutoAbstract to Presentation\</emph\> command. You must have formatted the headings with a corresponding Paragraph Style to be able to see this command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	id	Copying Text Using Drag-and-Drop				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303				0	id	If you select text and drag it into a spreadsheet with drag-and-drop, it will be inserted as text into the cell where you release the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	id	If you drag text to the normal view of a presentation, an OLE object is inserted as a $[officename] plug-in.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	id	If you drag the text to the outline view of a presentation, it will be inserted at the cursor location.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Adding Graphics to the Gallery				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Gallery; adding pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;adding to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;pictures in Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927	49			0	id	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Adding Graphics to the Gallery\"\>Adding Graphics to the Gallery\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	id	You can place a graphic from a document such as an HTML page in the Gallery by drag-and-drop.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	id	Display the Gallery theme to which you want to add the graphic.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	id	Position the mouse pointer above the graphic, without clicking.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	id	If the mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol, the graphic refers to a hyperlink. In this case, click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key to select it without executing the respective link.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	id	If the mouse pointer does not change to a hand symbol, you can simply click the graphic to select it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	id	Once the graphic is selected, release the mouse button. Click again on the graphic image, keeping the mouse button pressed for more than two seconds. The graphic image is copied to the internal memory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772				0	id	Without releasing the mouse button, drag the graphic into the Gallery.				20181231 09:50:43
