helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Error Report Tool				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150616				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>reports;error reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>crash reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>activating;Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	id	\<variable id=\"error_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\" name=\"Error Report Tool\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	id	The Error Report Tool starts automatically when a program crash occurs.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	id	The Error Report Tool gathers all necessary information that can help the program developers to improve the code, so that in later versions this error can possibly be avoided. Please help us to improve the software and send the generated error report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538				0	id	Starting the Error Report Tool				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	id	With most program crashes the Error Report Tool will start automatically.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154046				0	id	Completing the Report				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	id	On the main Error Report Tool dialog, you can enter some additional information that may help the developers to localize the error. For example, if the error only appears after a change in your hardware or software environment, or if you clicked on a button, please include that information.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399				0	id	Sending the Error Report				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	id	The Error Report Tool uses the HTTP PUT / SOAP protocol to send the report data. You may optionally enter some descriptive text that will help us to identify the context of the program crash. Then click the \<emph\>Send\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	id	You will not get an answer to your error report. If you need support, please visit the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\"\>support forum\</link\> on the Internet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	id	You may choose to respond to questions that the developers may have about the reported error. Mark the check box if you allow to be contacted by e-mail, should additional information be required. By default this box is not marked, so you will not get any e-mail.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	id	What Data is Sent?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	id	The error report consists of several files. The main file contains information about the error type, operating system name and version, memory usage, and the description that you entered. You can click the \<emph\>Show Report\</emph\> button on the main dialog of the Error Report Tool to view what will get sent in the main file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	id	In addition, relevant memory contents and stack traces are gathered by some system standard tools ("dbhhelp.dll" on Windows systems, "pstack" on UNIX systems). This information will be sent also.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>protecting; contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protected contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>contents protection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>encryption of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>passwords for protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>security;protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>form controls; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>graphics;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;protecting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	id	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	id	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	id	Protecting All Documents When Saving				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775				0	id	All documents that are saved in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\" name=\"OpenDocument format\"\>OpenDocument format\</link\> can be saved with a password. Documents that are saved with a password cannot be opened without the password. The content is secured so that it cannot be read with an external editor. This applies to content, graphics and OLE objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	id	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box. Save the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	id	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	id	Open the document, entering the correct password. Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	id	Information entered in \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\> is not encrypted. This includes the name of the author, creation date, word and character counts.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294				0	id	Protecting Revision Marking				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646				0	id	With every change made in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, the review function records who made the change. This function can be turned on with protection, so that it can only be turned off when the correct password is entered. Until then, all changes will continue to be recorded. Acceptance or rejection of changes is not possible.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	id	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	id	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter the correct password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155113				0	id	Protecting Frames, Graphics, and OLE Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703				0	id	You can protect the content, position and size of inserted graphics. The same applies to frames (in Writer) and OLE objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147131				0	id	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	id	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> and/or \<emph\>Size\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147510				0	id	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153657				0	id	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, unmark as appropriate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152992				0	id	Protecting Drawing Objects and Form Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	59			0	id	The draw objects that you insert into your documents with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar can be protected from being accidentally moved or changed in size. You can do the same with form objects inserted with the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153226				0	id	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815	61			0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Mark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289				0	id	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	63			0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Unmark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	id	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
