helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	id	\<variable id=\"textmode_change\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/textmode_change.xhp\" name=\"Switching Between Insert Mode and Overwrite Mode\"\>Switching Between Insert Mode and Overwrite Mode\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	id	Dengan papan ketik:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	3			0	id	Press Insert to toggle between overwrite mode and insert mode. The current mode is displayed on the Status Bar.\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\> The text cursor must be enabled in the cell or in the input line. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152349				0	id	Dengan tetikus:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	id	On the Status Bar, click on the area indicating the current mode in order to switch to the other mode:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	id	\<emph\>INSRT\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307	7			0	id	Insert mode is enabled. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The text cursor is a blinking vertical line. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>Click on the area to enable the overwrite mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	id	\<emph\>OVER\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491	9			0	id	The overwrite mode is enabled. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The text cursor is a blinking block. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>Click on the area to enable insert mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3154346				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/04/01010000.xhp\" name=\"Keyboard commands\"\>Keyboard commands\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154136				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>graphics, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting and editing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>illustrations, see pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pixel graphics; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invert filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>smoothing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sharpening filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remove noise filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>solarization filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aging filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>posterizing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pop-art filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charcoal sketches filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mosaic filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154136				0	id	\<variable id=\"insert_bitmap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_bitmap.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\"\>Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	id	Inserting Bitmaps				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	id	A bitmap image can be inserted in $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236				0	id	Select the file. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box you can restrict the selection to certain file types.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	id	Click the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box if you want a link to the original file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	id	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is marked, whenever the document is updated and loaded the bitmap image is reloaded. The editing steps that you have carried out in the local copy of the image in the document are re-applied and the image is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	id	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is not marked, you are always working with the copy created when the graphic was first inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	id	To embed graphics that were first inserted as links, go to \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Break Link\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	id	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the image.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	id	Editing Bitmaps				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id187078				0	id	Icons on the Picture bar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	id	When you select the bitmap image, the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar offers you the tools for editing the image. Only a local copy is edited in the document, even if you have inserted an image as a link.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	id	The \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar may look slightly different depending to the module you are using.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	13			0	id	A number of filters are located on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\" name=\"Graphic Filter\"\>Graphic \<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar, which you can open with the icon on the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7055574				0	id	The original picture file will not be changed by the filters. Filters are applied to a picture only inside the document. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	id	Some of the filters open a dialog, which you can use to select, for example, the intensity of the filter. Most filters can be applied multiple times to increase the filter effect.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	id	In $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress, you can add text and graphics, select these objects together with the bitmap, and export the selection as a new bitmap image.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id2572405				0	id	The Picture dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id6457411				0	id	Right-click the picture and choose \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> from the submenu to open a properties dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7991882				0	id	Change the properties of the selected picture, then click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153574				0	id	Saving Bitmaps				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	id	If you want to save in a format such as GIF, JPEG or TIFF, you must select and export the bitmap image.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803544667				0	id	To export a bitmap in Draw or Impress:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	id	Select the bitmap image. You can also select additional objects, such as text, to be exported with the image by pressing the shift key while selecting or by opening a selection frame around all objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> dialog opens.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3157139				0	id	The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> command writes the picture with all applied filter effects to a file. The \<emph\>Save as Picture\</emph\> command in the context menu saves the picture without any filter effects, if the picture was inserted as a linked picture. An embedded picture will always be saved or exported with filters applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	id	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> field, select the file format you want, for example GIF or JPEG.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	id	If you only want to export the selected objects, mark the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150874				0	id	If \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not marked, the entire page of the document is exported.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417				0	id	Enter a name for the file and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803525078				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To export a bitmap in Writer: Right-click the bitmap, choose Save Graphics. You see the Graphics Export dialog. Enter a file name and select a file type.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id1033051				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\"\>Graphic Filter Bar from the Picture Bar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>labels; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>business cards; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>synchronizing;labels and business cards\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	id	\<variable id=\"labels\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\"\>Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	id	Designing Business Cards Through a Dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	70			0	id	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Business Cards\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Business Cards\</emph\>\</link\> to open the\<emph\> Business Cards \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to choose how your business cards will look.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147654				0	id	Designing Labels and Business Cards				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	id	You can design both labels and business cards through the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	id	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010200.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Labels\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	id	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, define the label format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	id	$[officename] Writer contains many formats of commercially available sheets for labels, badges, and business cards. You can also add other, user-defined formats.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	id	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Inscription\</emph\>, you can choose what you want written on the labels.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	id	This often involves database fields, so that the labels can be printed with varying content, when sending "Form Letters" for example. It is also possible to have the same text printed on every label.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	85			0	id	Use the \<emph\>Database \</emph\>and \<emph\>Table \</emph\>list boxes to select the database and table from which the data fields are obtained. Click on the arrow button to transfer the selected data field into the inscription area. Press Enter to insert a line break. You can also enter spaces and any other fixed text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	id	On the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> tab you can define your own label formats, not covered by the predefined formats. To do this, select "User" from the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list box. On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, you can specify whether all labels or only certain ones are to be created.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	id	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, make sure that the \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> box is selected. If this is selected, a label only has to be entered (on the top left label) and edited once.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	id	As soon as you click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, you will see a small window with the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button. Enter the first label. When you click on the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button, the current individual label is copied to all the other labels on the sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	id	Click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\> to create a new document with the settings you have entered.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Business Cards\"\>Business Cards\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Inserting and Editing Tab Stops				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144436				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>tab stops; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;tab stops in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;tab stops on ruler\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rulers; default settings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rulers; measurement units\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>measurement units; changing on rulers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144436				0	id	\<variable id=\"tabs\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/tabs.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Tab Stops\"\>Inserting and Editing Tab Stops\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id1376079				0	id	On the horizontal ruler you can see the tab stops for the current paragraph. If you want to change the tab stops, you should first consider the scope to which you want to change tab stops as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id9434492				0	id	Change the default tab stops for all documents: Use the menu \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id274971				0	id	Change the tab stops for all paragraphs using the current Paragraph Style: Right-click the paragraph to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Tabs\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id5199133				0	id	Change the tab stops for one or more paragraphs: Select the paragraphs, then click inside the ruler.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id6178167				0	id	In the following, you find instructions for all above mentioned tasks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	27			0	id	You can set a tab stop by clicking on the ruler or by selecting \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Tabs.\</emph\> Both methods affect the current paragraph or all selected paragraphs.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	id	Click the ruler once to set a left-justified tab. Right-click a tab icon on the ruler to see the context menu in which you can change the tab type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	id	To set several decimal tabs one after the other, keep clicking the icon to the left of the ruler until the desired tab type is shown, then click on the ruler.				20181231 09:50:43
