helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	id	You can assign custom scripts (macros) to menu items, icons, dialog controls, and events in %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	id	%PRODUCTNAME internally supports the following scripting languages:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	id	%PRODUCTNAME Basic				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10739				0	id	JavaScript				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073D				0	id	BeanShell				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_id6797082				0	id	Python				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091F				0	id	In addition, developers can use high-level languages, for example Java programming language, to control %PRODUCTNAME externally. See the API project at Apache OpenOffice.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	id	To assign a script to a new menu entry				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Menus\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	id	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	id	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	id	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select a script.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10770				0	id	A list of the script functions appears in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> list box. Select a function.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	id	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to create a new menu assignment. The new menu entry appears in the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10783				0	id	To assign a script to a key combination				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10787				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Keyboard\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A59				0	id	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A61				0	id	You see entries for "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), "My Macros" (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A65				0	id	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select any script.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A69				0	id	A list of the script functions will appear in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> list box. Select any function.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A71				0	id	Click the option button for %PRODUCTNAME or Writer (or whichever application is currently open). 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A74				0	id	Selecting the option button sets the scope of the new key combination to be applicable in all of %PRODUCTNAME or only in documents of the current module.				20181231 09:50:43
