helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B87				0	id	Click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab of the Properties dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8B				0	id	Click one of the \<emph\>...\</emph\> buttons to open a dialog where you can assign a script to the selected event.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Printing Address Labels				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>address labels from databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>labels; from databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>stickers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>databases;creating labels\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	id	\<variable id=\"labels_database\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels_database.xhp\" name=\"Printing Address Labels\"\>Printing Address Labels\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	37			0	id	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab page, select the format of the label sheets you want to print on. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370863				0	id	Choose the database and table from which to get the data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id013020090337089				0	id	Select a database field of which you want to print the contents. Click the button that shows a left arrow to insert the database field into the Label Text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370930				0	id	Continue to select and insert database fields if you want more fields on every label. You can press Enter to insert a new line, and you can type any character to insert fixed text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370924				0	id	Optionally, if you want to type more text, apply formatting, or insert images and line art, you should enable \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab. If you enable this, once you leave the Labels dialog box a small window opens with a Synchronize button. Now you only need to work on the first label on the labels document, then click the Synchronize button to copy your work to every label of the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_idN10687				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Huruf\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	id	When you see the label document, you might want to temporarily enable \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Field Names\</item\>. This displays the fields in a more visible manner, so that you can arrange and edit label contents more easily.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148484				0	id	You can save and/or print the label document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id8476821				0	id	When you choose to print the document, you will be asked if you want to print a form letter. Answer Yes to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01150000.xhp\"\>Mail Merge\</link\> dialog. In the Mail Merge dialog, you can select the records for which you want to print labels.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Importing and Exporting Data in Base 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	bm_id6911546				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>databases;importing/exporting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; datasource records in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; datasource records in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;inserting database records\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;copying records to spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;from data sources to %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id4547257				0	id	\<variable id=\"data_im_export\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_im_export.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting Data in Base\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	id	An easy method to import and export database tables uses Calc as a "helper application".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3912778				0	id	Exporting data from Base				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	id	You copy a table from Base to a new Calc sheet, then you can save or export the data to any file format that Calc supports.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	id	Open the database file that contains the database table to be exported. Click Tables to view the tables, or click Queries to view the queries.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id4644306				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Spreadsheet\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	id	In the Base window, right-click the name of the table to export. Choose \<emph\>Copy\</emph\> from the context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	id	Click cell A1 in the new Calc window, then choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	id	Now you can save or export the data to many file types.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id9999694				0	id	Importing data to Base				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id8494521				0	id	You can import text files, spreadsheet files, and your system address book in read-only mode only. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id9579760				0	id	When you import from a text or spreadsheet file, the file must have a first row of header information. The second row of the file is the first valid data row. The format of every field in the second row determines the format for the entire column. Any format information from a spreadsheet file gets lost when importing to Base.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id325632				0	id	For example, to ensure the first column has a text format, you must make sure that the first field of the first valid data row contains text. If a field in the first valid data row contains a number, the whole column is set to number format, and only numbers, no text, will be shown in that column. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	id	Open a Base file of the database type that you want. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	id	Either create a new Base file using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz00.xhp\"\>Database Wizard\</link\>, or open any existing Base file that is not read-only.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	id	Open the Calc file that contains the data to be imported to Base. You can open a *.dbf dBASE file or many other file types. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	id	Select the data to be copied to Base. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id6173894				0	id	You can enter a range reference like A1:X500 in the Name Box if you don't want to scroll.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id533768				0	id	If you copy a dBASE sheet, include the top row that contains the header data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id5669423				0	id	Pilih \<emph\>Berkas - Buka\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3619495				0	id	In the Base window, click \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> to view the tables.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id1175572				0	id	In the Base window, choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id4815820				0	id	You see the Copy Table dialog. Most databases need a primary key, so you may want to check the \<emph\>Create primary key\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2584002				0	id	On Windows systems, you can also use drag-and-drop instead of Copy and Paste. Also, for registered databases, you can open the datasource browser (press F4) instead of opening the Base window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id5871761				0	id	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id6531266				0	id	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
