helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3154071	88			0	id	In the\<emph\> Toolbars \</emph\>box, select the toolbar you want to change.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	id	Click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\> , select the new command, then click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3152922	90			0	id	If you want, you can rearrange the \<emph\>Commands \</emph\>list by selecting a command name and clicking \<emph\>Move Up\</emph\> and \<emph\>Move Down\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\edit_symbolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Working with Groups 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id6888027				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>groups;entering/exiting/ungrouping\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; selection frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exiting;groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selection frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiple selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>marking, see selecting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id2454298				0	id	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/groups.xhp\"\>Working with Groups\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2307199				0	id	You can combine several graphic objects into a group so that you can use them like a single object. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9983825				0	id	You can move, transform, resize, distort, or convert all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group any time to change the individual objects. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id5734733				0	id	You can change the properties (line size, fill color, and more) of all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group and change the individual objects. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id561540				0	id	Groups can also be nested to form groups within other groups. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7705618				0	id	To group objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id607013				0	id	Select the objects together that you want to group. Hold down Shift while you click the individual objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	id	Right-click any of the selected objects to open the context menu. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	id	In Impress or Draw, choose Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group – Group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6738792				0	id	To select the objects, you can also drag a selection frame around the objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	id	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	id	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7424237				0	id	To enter a group				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	id	Right-click any object of the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	id	In Impress or Draw, choose Enter Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Edit Group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	id	Now you can select and edit a single object in the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	id	You can add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	id	The objects that are not part of the group are shown with dimmed colors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id9141819				0	id	To exit a group				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	id	Right-click any object of the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	id	In Impress or Draw, choose Exit Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Exit Group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	id	To exit a group in Draw or Impress, you can also double-click anywhere outside the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7889950				0	id	To ungroup a group				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	id	Right-click any object of the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	id	In Impress or Draw, choose Ungroup. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Ungroup.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	id	Now you can select and edit all objects as individual objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Copying Graphics From the Gallery				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145345				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>Gallery;dragging pictures to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;dropping Gallery pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;from Gallery to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	id	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_fromgallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics From the Gallery\"\>Copying Graphics From the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	id	If you drag a graphic from the Gallery into a text, spreadsheet or presentation document, the graphic will be inserted there.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	id	If you release the graphic \<emph\>directly on a draw object\</emph\>, please note the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	id	If you move the graphic (drag it without pressing any key, in which case no additional symbol appears next to the mouse pointer), only the attributes are copied from the graphic and applied to the draw object on which you release the mouse button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	id	If you copy the graphic (drag it while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, in which case a plus sign appears next to the mouse pointer), the graphic will be inserted as an object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	id	If you create a hyperlink (drag while holding down Shift and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, in which case a linking arrow appears next to the mouse pointer), the drawing object is replaced by the graphic from the Gallery, but the position and size of the replaced draw object are retained.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Languages Using Complex Text Layout				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153662				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>CTL;complex text layout languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>languages;complex text layout\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;CTL languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text layout for special languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right-to-left text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering text from right to left\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bi-directional writing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hindi;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hebrew;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Arabic;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Thai;entering text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662				0	id	\<variable id=\"ctl\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ctl.xhp\" name=\"Languages Using Complex Text Layout\"\>Languages Using Complex Text Layout\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	id	Currently, $[officename] supports Hindi, Thai, Hebrew, and Arabic as \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#ctl\" name=\"CTL languages\"\>CTL languages\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3155420				0	id	If you select the text flow from right to left, embedded Western text still runs from left to right. The cursor responds to the arrow keys in that Right Arrow moves it "to the text end" and Left Arrow "to the text start".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	id	You can change the text writing direction directly be pressing one of the following keys:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+D or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Right Shift Key - switch to right-to-left text entry				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+A or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Left Shift Key - switch to left-to-right text entry				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	id	The modifier-only key combinations only work when CTL support is enabled.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	id	In multicolumn pages, sections or frames that are formatted with text flow from right to left, the first column is the right column and the last column is the left column.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	id	In $[officename] Writer text formatted in \<emph\>Thai language\</emph\> has the following features:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	id	In paragraphs with justified alignment, the characters are stretched to flush the lines at the margins. In other languages the spaces between words are stretched.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	id	Use the Delete key to delete a whole composite character. Use the Backspace key to delete the last part of the previous composite character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809				0	id	Use the Right or Left Arrow key to jump to the next or previous whole composite character. To position the cursor into a composite character, use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>Language Settings - Languages\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
