helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145075				0	id	Controlling the ImageMap Editor				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159096				0	id	Press Tab to select an icon. If you selected one of the icons from \<emph\>Rectangle\</emph\> to \<emph\>Freeform Polygon\</emph\> and you press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter, an object of the selected type is created in default size.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156016				0	id	If you press Enter while the icon \<emph\>Select\</emph\> is selected, the focus is set into the image window of the ImageMap Editor. Press Esc to set the focus back to the icons and input boxes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587				0	id	If the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon is selected and you press Ctrl+Enter, the first object in the image window gets selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154343				0	id	Use the icon \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> to switch into the point edit mode for polygons and back.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147073				0	id	Use Ctrl+Tab in the image window to select the next point. Use Shift+Ctrl+Tab to select the previous point.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153285				0	id	Use the Delete key with the focus in the image window to delete the selected object.				20181231 09:50:43
