helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Using Toolbars				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>toolbars;docking/undocking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>toolbars;viewing/closing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>closing;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>docking;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fixing toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>detaching toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>placing toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>positioning;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attaching toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>floating toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows;docking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>icon bars, see toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>button bars, see toolbars\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	id	\<variable id=\"floating_toolbar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/floating_toolbar.xhp\" name=\"Using Toolbars\"\>Using Toolbars\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	id	Some toolbar icons, for example the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, can open another toolbar. Click the arrow next to the icon to open a toolbar containing further icons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450	8			0	id	You now have a choice: either click the icon that you want to activate, or seize the toolbar by its title bar and drag it while holding down the mouse button. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id733970				0	id	Context of Toolbars				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id341196				0	id	Some toolbars open automatically depending on the context. For example, when you click inside a table in a text document, the Table toolbar opens. When you click inside a numbered paragraph, the Bullets and Numbering toolbar opens.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id4224372				0	id	To Close a Toolbar Temporarily				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id295724				0	id	Click the icon in the toolbar's title bar, or choose \<emph\>Close Toolbar\</emph\> from the context menu. The toolbar will be shown automatically again when the context becomes active again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id1905575				0	id	To Close a Toolbar Permanently				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id9776909				0	id	While the toolbar is visible, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars\</emph\> and click the name of the toolbar to remove the check mark.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	id	To Show a Closed Toolbar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	id	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars\</emph\> and click the name of the toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id7296975				0	id	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Reset\</emph\> to reset the toolbars to their default context sensitive behavior. Now some toolbars will be shown automatically, dependent on the context.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E9				0	id	To Make a Toolbar a Floating Toolbar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EF				0	id	Click the handle at the start of the toolbar, and drag the toolbar into the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	id	To Reattach a Floating Toolbar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F7				0	id	Drag the title bar of the toolbar to an edge of the document window. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id6154362				0	id	To reattach a floating window, drag-and-drop the window's title bar to an edge of the document window. The mouse pointer should be very close to the document window's edge when you release the mouse button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id1510055				0	id	Depending on your system's window manager settings, you may also double-click an empty place on the toolbar or window, while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. Or double-click the title bar of the floating toolbar or window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AC				0	id	Docking toolbars and windows by drag-and-drop depends on your system's window manager settings. You must enable your system to show the full window contents when you move a window, instead of showing just the outer frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Opening Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147834				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>opening; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;creating/opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations;creating/opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FTP; opening documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>new documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>empty documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;creating/opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; creating/opening\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; new\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147834				0	id	\<variable id=\"doc_open\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_open.xhp\" name=\"Opening Documents\"\>Opening Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	id	Opening an existing document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	id	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A9				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	id	Click the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> icon on the Standard toolbar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	id	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+O 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	id	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	id	Select the file you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149234				0	id	Restrict Files to Display				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	id	To restrict the display of files in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog to a certain type select the corresponding \<emph\>File type\</emph\> from the list. Select \<emph\>All Files (*.*)\</emph\> to display all files.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id4651326				0	id	Cursor Position				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id5509201				0	id	In general, all documents open with the cursor at the start of the document. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id6594744				0	id	One exception appears when the author of a Writer text document saves and reopens a document: The cursor will be at the same position where it has been when the document was saved. This only works when the name of the author was entered in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - User Data\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3422650				0	id	Press Shift+F5 to set the cursor to the last saved position.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148453				0	id	Opening an Empty Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	id	Click the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar or choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>. This opens a document of the document type specified.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	id	If you click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon, a submenu opens in which you can select another document type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501358				0	id	System File Dialogs or %PRODUCTNAME Dialogs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501356				0	id	On most operating systems, you can choose to use the system file dialogs or %PRODUCTNAME dialogs.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501429				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\> to switch the type of open/save dialogs.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501449				0	id	The %PRODUCTNAME dialogs support file download and upload using secure https connections.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501453				0	id	Opening Files from a Web Server				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	9			0	id	You can enter a URL in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialogs. The URL must start with file:/// or ftp:// or http://. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501548				0	id	If you use the %PRODUCTNAME dialog, you can use the https:// prefix for a secure connection, and you can save a document on the web server.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C4				0	id	When you open a file by a URL from the Windows file dialog, Windows will open a local copy of the file, located in the Internet Explorer cache. The %PRODUCTNAME file dialog opens a local copy of the file in the system's temp folder.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Recording and Displaying Changes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>marking changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changes; review function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>review function; recording changes example\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Track Changes, see review function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	id	\<variable id=\"redlining\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining.xhp\" name=\"Recording and Displaying Changes\"\>Recording and Displaying Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	id	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	id	When several authors are working on the same text or spreadsheet, the review function records and displays who made the various changes. On the final edit of the document, it is then possible to look at each individual change and decide whether it should be accepted or rejected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	id	For example: You are an editor and are delivering your latest report. But before publication the report must be read by the senior editor and the proofreader, and both will add their changes. The senior editor writes "clarify" after one paragraph and crosses out another entirely. The proofreader corrects the spelling of your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	id	The edited document comes back to you, and you can incorporate or ignore the suggestions of the two reviewers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	id	Let's say you also e-mailed a copy of the report to a good friend and colleague who has done research on a similar topic in the past. You asked for a few suggestions, and the document is now returned by e-mail with your colleague's suggestions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	id	As all your colleagues and the managers in your company work with $[officename], you can produce a final version of the document from the results you get back.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Collaboration				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	bm_id4459669				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>sharing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>collaboration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>file locking with collaboration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>locked documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id130008				0	id	\<variable id=\"collab\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/collab.xhp\"\>Collaboration\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5821710				0	id	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, Impress, and Draw, only one user at a time can open any document for writing. In Calc, many users can open the same spreadsheet for writing at the same time.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9590136				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Share Document dialog where you can enable or disable collaborative sharing of the document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2519913				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enable to share the current document with other users. Disable to use the document unshared. This will invalidate the not yet saved edits that other users applied in the time since you last opened or saved this document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id6917020				0	id	Collaboration in Calc				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id4411145				0	id	In %PRODUCTNAME Calc, document sharing allows simultaneous write access for many users. Every user who wants to collaborate should enter a name on the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - %PRODUCTNAME - User Data\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6799218				0	id	Some commands are not available (grayed out) when change tracking or document sharing is activated. For a new spreadsheet you cannot apply or insert the grayed out elements. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id3274941				0	id	Creating a new spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9804681				0	id	User A creates a new spreadsheet document. The following conditions can apply:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2109744				0	id	The user does not want to share the spreadsheet for collaboration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5374614				0	id	User A opens, edits, and saves the document as described above for Writer, Impress, and Draw document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id768761				0	id	The user wants to share the document for collaboration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6844691				0	id	The user chooses \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Share Document\</item\> to activate the collaboration features for this document. A dialog opens where the user can choose to enable or disable sharing. If the user enables sharing, the document will be saved in shared mode, which is also shown on the title bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5288857				0	id	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Share Document\</item\> command can be used to switch the mode for the current document from unshared mode to shared mode. If you want to use a shared document in unshared mode, you would save the shared document using another name or path. This creates a copy of the spreadsheet that is not shared.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id8842127				0	id	Opening a spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7276528				0	id	User A opens a spreadsheet document. The following conditions can apply:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id8363902				0	id	The spreadsheet document is not in shared mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	id	The user can open, edit, and save the document as described above for Writer, Impress, and Draw documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5323343				0	id	The spreadsheet document is in shared mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5824457				0	id	The user sees a message that the document is in shared mode and that some features are not available in this mode. The user can disable this message for the future. After clicking OK, the document is opened in shared mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5800653				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If the same contents are changed by different users, the Resolve Conflicts dialog opens. For each conflict, decide which changes to keep.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6263924				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps your change, voids the other change.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id3609118				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps the change of the other user, voids your change.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7184057				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps all your changes, voids all other changes.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id786767				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps the changes of all other users, voids your changes.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id2934965				0	id	Saving a shared spreadsheet document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id1174657				0	id	User A saves a shared document. The following conditions can apply:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2577593				0	id	The document was not modified and saved by another user since user A opened the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5883968				0	id	The document is saved.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9049653				0	id	The document was modified and saved by another user since user A opened the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id1976683				0	id	If the changes do not conflict, the document is saved.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id43946				0	id	If the changes conflict, the Resolve Conflicts dialog will be shown. User A must decide for the conflicts which version to keep, "Keep Mine" or "Keep Other". When all conflicts are resolved, the document is saved. While user A resolves the conflicts, no other user is able to save the shared document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6449171				0	id	Another user tries to save the shared document and resolves conflicts in this moment.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7101046				0	id	User A sees a message that a merge-in is in progress. User A can choose to cancel the save command for now, or retry saving some time later.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7186498				0	id	When a user successfully saves a shared spreadsheet, the document will be reloaded after the save command, so that the spreadsheet shows the latest version of all changes that got saved by all users. A message shows that "foreign changes have been added" when another user did change some contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id2871791				0	id	Collaboration in Writer, Impress, and Draw				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2675862				0	id	For all modules Writer, Impress, Draw, and for Calc when document sharing is not enabled, a file locking is possible. This file locking is available even when accessing the same document from different operating systems:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7333597				0	id	User A opens a document. The following conditions can apply:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9976195				0	id	The document is not locked by any other user.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2507400				0	id	This document will be opened for read and write access by user A. The document will be locked for other users until user A closes the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id216681				0	id	The document is marked as "read-only" by the file system.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7709585				0	id	This document will be opened in read-only mode. Editing is not allowed. User A can save the document using another document name or another path. User A can edit this copy.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id4309518				0	id	The document is locked by another user.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id206610				0	id	User A sees a dialog that tells the user the document is locked. The dialog offers to open the document in read-only mode, or to open a copy for editing, or to cancel the Open command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id29349651				0	id	User access permissions and sharing documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id11746571				0	id	Some conditions must be met on operating systems with a user permission management.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id25775931				0	id	The shared file needs to reside in a location which is accessible by all collaborators.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id90496531				0	id	The file permissions for both the document and the corresponding lock file need to be set so that all collaborators can create, delete, and change the files.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id71864981				0	id	Write access also enables other users to (accidentally or deliberately) delete or change a file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id4263740				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Working with Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id1983703				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table views of databases\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	id	\<variable id=\"data_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tables.xhp\"\>Working with Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	id	Data is stored in tables. As an example, your system address book that you use for your e-mail addresses is a table of the address book database. Each address is a data record, presented as a row in that table. The data records consist of data fields, for example the first and the last name fields and the e-mail field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	id	Creating a New Table With the Table Wizard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	id	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new table using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard00.xhp\"\>Table Wizard\</link\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	id	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	id	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	id	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Table\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	id	Creating a New Table With the Design View				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	id	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	id	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	id	Click \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	id	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\"\>Table Design\</link\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	id	Creating a New Table View				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077C				0	id	Some database types support table views. A table view is a query that is stored with the database. For most database operations, a view can be used as you would use a table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10782				0	id	Open the database file where you want to create the new table view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	id	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078E				0	id	Click \<emph\>Create Table View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10795				0	id	You see the View Design window, which is almost the same as the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
