helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Creating XML Filters 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>testing XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XML filters;creating/testing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id1413922				0	id	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_create.xhp\"\>Creating XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053D				0	id	Creating an XML Filter for %PRODUCTNAME				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109A9				0	id	When you create an XML filter for %PRODUCTNAME, you need to design an \<emph\>XSLT stylesheet\</emph\> that can convert to and from the OpenDocument XML file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B0				0	id	For more information about the OpenDocument XML format, go to \<link href=\"https://xml.openoffice.org/\"\>https://xml.openoffice.org/\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C5				0	id	If you want, you can include a \<emph\>template\</emph\> with your filter to apply %PRODUCTNAME styles to an XML document that you import.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CC				0	id	You can also include the \<emph\>Document Type Definition\</emph\> (DTD) for the external XML format so you can validate the XML format, for example, when you test the filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10531				0	id	To Create an XML Filter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E0				0	id	Create an XSLT transformation \<emph\>stylesheet\</emph\> that maps the elements of the external XML format to the elements of the OpenDocument XML file format and back again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	id	Create a template that assigns %PRODUCTNAME styles to elements in the external XML format when you import a file in this format into %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	id	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, create a text document, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109F4				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109FC				0	id	In the \<emph\>XML Filter\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and define the properties of the filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A03				0	id	In the \<emph\>Filter Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the XML filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CA1				0	id	This name is displayed in the \<emph\>XML Filter Settings\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A09				0	id	In the \<emph\>Application\</emph\> box, select the %PRODUCTNAME application that the filter is for.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0F				0	id	In the \<emph\>Name of File Type\</emph\> box, enter the file type that the filter is for.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	id	This name is displayed in the list of file types in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\>, \<emph\>Export\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogs.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A15				0	id	In the \<emph\>File extension\</emph\> box, enter the extension for the exported file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1B				0	id	To differentiate the file from other XML files, enter an extension other than *.xml.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1F				0	id	On the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page, define the transformation properties for the filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	id	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DocType\</emph\> box, enter the document type identifier for the external file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D0E				0	id	This identifier is used to detect the file type on import.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A2C				0	id	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DTD\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the DTD for the external file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D1F				0	id	This DTD is used to validate the files on export.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A32				0	id	In the \<emph\>XSLT for export\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from OpenDocument format to the external format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A38				0	id	In the \<emph\>XSLT for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name to the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from the external format to OpenDocument format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3E				0	id	(Optional) In the \<emph\>Template for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and name of the template that defines the %PRODUCTNAME styles that are used in the imported file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A44				0	id	The files that are specified on the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page are copied to the local %PRODUCTNAME users directory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A4C				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A56				0	id	To Test an XML Filter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A5A				0	id	You can perform basic tests on a custom XML filter in %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A91				0	id	The document is not altered by these tests. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A60				0	id	Create or open a text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A67				0	id	Pilih \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Perkakas - Pengaturan Penyaring XML\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A6F				0	id	In the list of filters, select the filter that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Test XSLTs\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A82				0	id	To test an \<emph\>Export\</emph\> Filter, do one of the following in the \<emph\>Export\</emph\> area of the dialog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DEB				0	id	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>, select the %PRODUCTNAME document that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DF7				0	id	To test the current document, click \<emph\>Current Document\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A99				0	id	To test an \<emph\>Import\</emph\> Filter, click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> area of the dialog, select a document, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E32				0	id	To validate the transformed file against the specified DTD, click \<emph\>Validate\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_id8579668				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>About XML Filters\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_id5569017				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_distribute.xhp\"\>Distributing XML filters\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Creating Round Corners				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150040				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>corner roundings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rectangles with round corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>legends;rounding corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>round corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customizing;round corners\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	id	\<variable id=\"round_corner\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/round_corner.xhp\" name=\"Creating Round Corners\"\>Creating Round Corners\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	id	When you insert a rectangle or a callout box using the drawing functions and activate the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, you see a small frame at the upper left corner of the object. The frame indicates the amount by which the corners are rounded. When the frame is positioned at the top left corner, no rounding occurs. When the frame is positioned on the handle centered at the top of the object, the corners are rounded as much as possible. You adjust the degree of rounding by moving the frame between these two positions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id3150774\" src=\"res/helpimg/hand01.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150774\"\>Mouse pointer as hand\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539				0	id	If you place the cursor on the box it changes to a hand symbol. You can now drag the box to change the amount of rounding. An outline shows a preview of the result.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143267				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Internet; Internet Explorer for displaying $[officename] documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] documents;viewing and editing in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	id	\<variable id=\"activex\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/activex.xhp\" name=\"ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\"\>ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	id	Under Windows only, you can view any $[officename] document in a window of the Microsoft Internet Explorer. Install the ActiveX control in the $[officename] Setup program.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156346				0	id	Installing the ActiveX control				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	id	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	id	Click the Start button on the Windows taskbar. Choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	id	In the Control Panel, click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	id	In the list, click %PRODUCTNAME, then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	id	In the Installation Wizard, select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	id	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry and find the \<emph\>ActiveX Control\</emph\> entry. Open the sub menu of the icon and select to install the feature.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	8			0	id	Klik \<emph\>Lanjut\</emph\> dan \<emph\>Pasang\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	id	Menampilkan dokumen $[officename]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	id	In Internet Explorer, browse to a web page that contains a link to a $[officename] Writer document, for example.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	id	Click the link to view the document in the Internet Explorer window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154072				0	id	You may still right-click the link to save the file on your harddisk.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	id	Menyunting dokumen $[officename]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154367				0	id	The $[officename] document inside the Internet Explorer shows a set of read-only toolbar icons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	id	Click the \<emph\>Edit file\</emph\> icon in the document's toolbar to open a copy of the document in a new $[officename] window.				20181231 09:50:43
