helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editors; ImageMap editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>images; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hotspots;adding to images\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;in pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	id	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	id	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	id	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	id	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	id	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	id	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	id	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	id	You can see an extended help text on the functions of each icon when you enable Extended Help in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	id	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	id	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	id	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	id	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				20181231 09:50:43
