helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\" name=\"Calculate\"\>Calculate\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines the calculation settings for spreadsheets.\</ahelp\> Defines the behavior of spreadsheets with iterative references, the date settings, the number of decimal places, and if capitalization or lower cases are to be considered when searching within sheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149399				0	id	Iterative references				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	id	In this section you can delimit the number of approximation steps carried out during iterative calculations. In addition, you can specify the degree of precision of the answer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154142				0	id	Iterations				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795	6			0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_ITERATE\"\>Specifies whether formulas with iterative references (formulas that are continuously repeated until the problem is solved) are calculated after a specific number of repetitions.\</ahelp\> If the\<emph\> Iterations \</emph\>box is not marked, an iterative reference in the table will cause an error message.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686	7			0	id	         \<emph\>Example:\</emph\> calculating the cost of an item without the value-added tax.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	id	Type the text 'Selling price' in cell A5, the text 'Net' in cell A6, and the text 'Value-added tax' in cell A7.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530	61			0	id	Now type a selling price (for example, 100) in cell B5. The net price should be shown in cell B6 and the value-added tax should be shown in cell B7. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153061				0	id	You know that the value-added tax is calculated as 'net price times 15%' and that you arrive at the net price by deducting the value-added tax from the selling price. Type the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=B5-B7\</item\> in B6 to calculate the net price, and type the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=B6*0.15\</item\> in cell B7 to calculate the value-added tax.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	id	Switch on the iterations to correctly calculate the formulas, otherwise a 'Circular reference' error message appears in the \<emph\>Status\</emph\> Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
