helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148814	44			0	id	If \<emph\>Search criteria = and <> must apply to whole cells \</emph\>is not enabled, the "win" search pattern acts like ".*win.*". The search pattern can be at any position within the cell when searching with the Calc database functions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156448				0	id	Enable regular expressions in formulas				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155092				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_CHECKBOX_RID_SCPAGE_CALC_BTN_REGEX\"\>Specifies that regular expressions are enabled when searching and also for character string comparisons.\</ahelp\>\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\> This relates to the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060101.xhp\" name=\"database functions\"\>database functions\</link\>, and to VLOOKUP, HLOOKUP and SEARCH.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156199				0	id	Automatically find column and row labels				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCPAGE_CALC:BTN_LOOKUP\"\>Specifies that you can use the text in any cell as a label for the column below the text or the row to the right of the text. The text must consist of at least one word and must not contain any operators.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242	57			0	id	         \<emph\>Example\</emph\>: Cell E5 contains the text "Europe". Below, in cell E6, is the value 100 and in cell E7 the value 200. If the \<emph\>Automatically find column and row labels\</emph\> box is marked, you can write the following formula in cell A1: =SUM(Europe).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	hd_id315634199				0	id	Limit decimals for general number format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id315343818				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>You can specify the maximum number of decimal places that are shown by default for cells with General number format. If not enabled, cells with General number format show as many decimal places as the column width allows.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
