helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id8257087				0	id	Select the format for the page numbers, either "Page N" or "Page N of M", where N stands for the current page number, and M for the total number of pages in the report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3479415				0	id	Select to show the page numbers in the Page Header area or in the Page Footer area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4441663				0	id	Select an alignment. By default the page numbers are centered between the left and right margins. You can align the field to the left or right. You can also select Inside to print page number on odd pages on the left side and even page numbers on the right side. Select Outside for the opposite alignment.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3012176				0	id	When you click OK, a data field for the page numbers is inserted. If no header or footer area exist, the area will be created as needed.				20181231 09:50:43
