helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Replaces named parameters in a data source with a question mark (?).\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D2				0	id	Display version columns (when available)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D6				0	id	Some databases assign version numbers to fields to track changes to records. The version number of a field is incremented by one each time the contents of the field are changed. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_SUPPRESS_VERSIONCL\"\>Displays the internal version number of the record in the database table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FA				0	id	Use the catalog name in SELECT statements				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FE				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Uses the current data source of the catalog. This option is useful when the ODBC data source is a database server. Do not select this option if the ODBC data source is a dBASE driver.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10613				0	id	Use the schema name in SELECT statements				20181231 09:50:43
