helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154660				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>MathML; import from file\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659				0	id	Import Formula from File				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150251				0	id	\<variable id=\"formelimportierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ImportFormula\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This command opens a dialog for importing a formula.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916				0	id	The \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> dialog is set up like the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog under \<emph\>File\</emph\>. Use the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> dialog to load, edit and display a formula saved as a file in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153917				0	id	You can import MathML files created by other applications as well. The MathML source must have a \<item type=\"code\"\>math\</item\> element with an \<item type=\"code\"\>xmlns\</item\> attribute with value "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML". The languages MathML and StarMath are not fully compatible, therefore you should revise the import result. For details about the language MathML see its \<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/TR/#tr_MathML\"\>specification\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154661				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>MathML; import via clipboard\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154662				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>importing; MathML\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154661				0	id	Import MathML from Clipboard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150252				0	id	\<variable id=\"mathmlimportierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ImportMathMLClipboard\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This command transforms MathML clipboard content to StarMath and inserts it at the current cursor position.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153918				0	id	If the transformation fails, nothing is inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	id	This command handles only MathML content. If you have copied a %PRODUCTNAME Math formula to clipboard, insert it using the command \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02060000.xhp\" name=\"Paste\"\>Paste\</link\> under \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
