helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id4901272				0	id	\<variable id=\"show\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/show.xhp\" name=\"Showing a Slide Show\"\>Showing a Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9636829				0	id	Different ways exist to start a slide show. Once a slide show is running, you can take control pressing keys or clicking the mouse buttons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id7076937				0	id	By default, a slide show always starts with the first slide. You advance manually through slides up to the last slide. You can change these settings.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id9954527				0	id	Selama Pertunjukan Slide				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6860255				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show\</emph\> to run the show.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4199957				0	id	If you want all shows to start from the current slide instead of the first slide, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3209936				0	id	Click to advance to the next effect or to the next slide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8702658				0	id	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to abort the show before the end.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3741264				0	id	Many more keys are available to \<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\"\>control a slide show\</link\>. You can also right-click to open a context menu with useful commands.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id5694143				0	id	Showing an automatic slide show (kiosk mode)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id5829645				0	id	For an automatic change to the next slide, you must assign a slide transition to each slide. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id2361522				0	id	On the Task Pane, click \<emph\>Slide Transition\</emph\> to open that tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9168980				0	id	In the \<emph\>Advance slide\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Automatically after\</emph\>, and select a time duration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9766533				0	id	Click \<emph\>Apply to All Slides\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	id	You can assign a different time for every slide to advance to the next slide. The \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\"\>rehearse timings\</link\> feature can assist you to get the timing right.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9219641				0	id	To advance to the first slide, after all slides have been shown, you must set the slide show to repeat automatically.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3174230				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1336405				0	id	In the Type area, click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and select a pause time between shows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4959257				0	id	When you create a new slide show using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01050000.xhp\"\>Presentation Wizard\</link\>, you can select the duration of slides and of the pause, on the third wizard page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id1906491				0	id	Running a slide show from a file				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	id	You can start %PRODUCTNAME from a command prompt, followed by the parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>-show\</item\> and an Impress filename. For example, to start the file \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> from the command prompt, enter the following command:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1502121				0	id	\<item type=\"literal\"\>soffice -show filename.odp\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	id	This assumes that soffice is in the program path of your system, and that \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> is located in the current directory.				20181231 09:50:43
