helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	3			0	id	Lapisan tersedia pada $[officename] Draw, bukan di $[officename] Impress. Dengan lapisan, Anda bisa menyusun elemen-elemen pada halaman yang berhubungan. Bayangkanlah lapisan itu sebagai ruang kerja yang saling terpisah yang bisa Anda sembunyikan dari tampilan layar, sembunyikan dari pencetakan, atau dikunci.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id7036957				0	id	Layers do not determine the stacking order of objects on your page, except for the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer which is always in front of other layers. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id1614734				0	id	The stacking order of objects on your page is determined by the sequence in which you add the objects. You can rearrange the stacking order by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id398876				0	id	Wilayah pada lapisan yang tidak mengandung objek satu pun adalah wilayah yang transparan.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	id	$[officename] Draw menyediakan tiga lapisan dasar:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	id	Tataletak				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	id	Kontrol				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	id	Garis Dimensi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156397				0	id	Anda tidak bisa menghapus atau mengubah nama lapisan yang disediakan oleh sistem. Anda bisa menambah lapisan Anda sendiri dengan \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sisip - Lapisan\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	id	The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer is the default workspace. The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer determines the location of title, text, and object placeholders on your page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	id	The \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer can be used for buttons that have been assigned an action, but that should not be printed. Set the layer's properties to not printable. Objects on the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer are always in front of objects on other layers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	id	The \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\> layer is where you draw, for example, the dimension lines. By switching the layer to show or hide, you can easily switch these lines on and off.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507				0	id	You can lock a layer to protect its contents, or hide a layer and its contents from view or from printing. When you add a new layer to a page, the layer is added to all of the pages in your document. However, when you add an object to a layer, it is only added to the current page. If you want the object to appear on all of the pages, add the object to the master page (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Master\</item\>).				20181231 09:50:43
