helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Consolidating Data				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>consolidating data\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ranges; combining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>combining;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; combining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data; merging cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;data ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	id	\<variable id=\"consolidate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/consolidate.xhp\" name=\"Consolidating Data\"\>Consolidating Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	id	During consolidation, the contents of the cells from several sheets will be combined in one place.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id892056				0	id	To Combine Cell Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	id	Open the document that contains the cell ranges to be consolidated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Consolidate\</item\> to open the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	id	From the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\> box select a source cell range to consolidate with other areas.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	id	If the range is not named, click in the field next to the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\>. A blinking text cursor appears. Type a reference for the first source data range or select the range with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	id	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert the selected range in the \<emph\>Consolidation areas\</emph\> field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153816				0	id	Select additional ranges and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> after each selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157983				0	id	Specify where you want to display the result by selecting a target range from the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215				0	id	If the target range is not named, click in the field next to \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> and enter the reference of the target range. Alternatively, you can select the range using the mouse or position the cursor in the top left cell of the target range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813				0	id	Select a function from the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> box. The function specifies how the values of the consolidation ranges are linked. The "Sum" function is the default setting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149315				0	id	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to consolidate the ranges.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	id	Additional Settings				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250				0	id	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog to display additional settings:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156400				0	id	Select \<emph\>Link to source data\</emph\> to insert the formulas that generate the results in the target range, rather than the actual results. If you link the data, any values modified in the source range are automatically updated in the target range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	id	The corresponding cell references in the target range are inserted in consecutive rows, which are automatically ordered and then hidden from view. Only the final result, based on the selected function, is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945				0	id	Under \<emph\>Consolidate by\</emph\>, select either \<emph\>Row labels\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column labels\</emph\> if the cells of the source data range are not to be consolidated corresponding to the identical position of the cell in the range, but instead according to a matching row label or column label.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	id	To consolidate by row labels or column labels, the label must be contained in the selected source ranges.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150478				0	id	The text in the labels must be identical, so that rows or columns can be accurately matched. If the row or column label does not match any that exist in the target range, it will be appended as a new row or column.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468				0	id	The data from the consolidation ranges and target range will be saved when you save the document. If you later open a document in which consolidation has been defined, this data will again be available.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153039				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Consolidate\"\>Data - Consolidate\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Only Copy Visible Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150440				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>cells; copying/deleting/formatting/moving\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows;visible and invisible\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>moving;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>invisible cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>filters;copying visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hidden cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	id	\<variable id=\"cellcopy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellcopy.xhp\" name=\"Only Copy Visible Cells\"\>Only Copy Visible Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	id	Assume you have hidden a few rows in a cell range. Now you want to copy, delete, or format only the remaining visible rows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	id	$[officename] behavior depends on how the cells were made invisible, by a filter or manually.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	id	Metode dan Aksi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150751				0	id	Hasil				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	id	Cells were filtered by AutoFilters, standard filters or advanced filters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	id	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	id	Only the visible cells of the selection are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3166427				0	id	Cells were hidden using the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> command in the context menu of the row or column headers, or through an \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"outline\"\>outline\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	id	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	id	All cells of the selection, including the hidden cells, are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Entering Formulas 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>formula bar; input line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input line in formula bar\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; inputting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	id	\<variable id=\"formula_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Formulas\"\>Entering Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6848353				0	id	You can enter formulas in several ways: using the icons, or by typing on the keyboard, or by a mixture of both methods.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	id	Click the cell in which you want to enter the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	id	Click the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> icon on the Formula Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	id	You will now see an equals sign in the input line and you can begin to input the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	id	After entering the required values, press Enter or click \<emph\>Accept\</emph\> to insert the result in the active cell. If you want to clear your entry in the input line, press Escape or click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	id	You can also enter the values and the formulas directly into the cells, even if you cannot see an input cursor. Formulas must always begin with an equals sign.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id4206976				0	id	You can also press the + or - key on the numerical keyboard to start a formula. NumLock must be "on". For example, press the following keys in succession:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	id	+ 5 0 - 8 Enter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8171330				0	id	You see the result \<item type=\"literal\"\>42\</item\> in the cell. The cell contains the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=+50-8\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	id	If you are editing a formula with references, the references and the associated cells will be highlighted with the same color. You can now resize the reference border using the mouse, and the reference in the formula displayed in the input line also changes. \<emph\>Show references in color\</emph\> can be deactivated under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210	7			0	id	\<variable id=\"tip\"\>If you would like to view the calculation of individual elements of a formula, select the respective elements and press F9. For example, in the formula =SUM(A1:B12)*SUM(C1:D12) select the section SUM(C1:D12) and press F9 to view the subtotal for this area. \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	id	If an error occurs when creating the formula, an \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error message\"\>error message\</link\> appears in the active cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Formula bar\"\>Formula bar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Memilih Banyak Sel				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>cells; selecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>marking cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple cells selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selection modes in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; selecting ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	id	\<variable id=\"mark_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/mark_cells.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Multiple Cells\"\>Selecting Multiple Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	id	Select a rectangular range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261				0	id	With the mouse button pressed, drag from one corner to the diagonally opposed corner of the range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	id	Mark a single cell				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	id	Lakukan salah satu langkah berikut:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	id	Click, then Shift-click the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	id	Pressing the mouse button, drag a range across two cells, do not release the mouse button, and then drag back to the first cell. Release the mouse button. You can now move the individual cell by drag and drop.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942				0	id	Select various dispersed cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072060				0	id	Lakukan salah satu langkah berikut:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	id	Mark at least one cell. Then while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, click each of the additional cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072023				0	id	Click the STD / EXT / ADD area in the status bar until it shows ADD. Now click all cells that you want to select.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	id	Switch marking mode				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	id	On the status bar, click the box with the legend STD / EXT / ADD to switch the marking mode:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264				0	id	Field contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	id	Effect of clicking the mouse				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	id	STD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3148486				0	id	A mouse click selects the cell you have clicked on. Unmarks all marked cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	id	EXT				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150305				0	id	A mouse click marks a rectangular range from the current cell to the cell you clicked. Alternatively, Shift-click a cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	id	ADD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	id	A mouse click in a cell adds it to the already marked cells. A mouse click in a marked cell unmarks it. Alternatively, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click the cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0208.xhp\" name=\"baris Status\"\>baris Status\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Defining Database Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154758				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>tables; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>database ranges; defining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ranges; defining database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;database ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154758				0	id	\<variable id=\"database_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Database Ranges\"\>Defining a Database Range\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	id	You can define a range of cells in a spreadsheet to use as a database. Each row in this database range corresponds to a database record and each cell in a row corresponds to a database field. You can sort, group, search, and perform calculations on the range as you would in a database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801	82			0	id	You can only edit and access a database range in the spreadsheet that contains the range. You cannot access the database range in the %PRODUCTNAME Data Sources view. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10648				0	id	To define a database range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	id	Select the range of cells that you want to define as a database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10654				0	id	Pilih \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Menentukan Jangkauan\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153715				0	id	In the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066A				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	id	Specify the options for the database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10675				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Menerapkan Banyak Operasi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154759				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; selecting multiple\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>appending sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154759				0	id	\<variable id=\"multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multitables.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Sheets\"\>Applying Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576				0	id	Inserting a Sheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Sheet\</item\> to insert a new sheet or an existing sheet from another file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203598				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog box where you can assign macros to sheet events.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203523				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a window where you can assign a color to the sheet tab.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id050920091402035				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to select all sheets in the document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914020391				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to deselect all sheets in the document, except the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	id	Memilih Banyak Sel				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	id	The sheet tab of the current sheet is always visible in white in front of the other sheet tabs. The other sheet tabs are gray when they are not selected. By clicking other sheet tabs while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>you can select multiple sheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	id	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600				0	id	Undoing a Selection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	id	To undo the selection of a sheet, click its sheet tab again while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. The sheet that is currently visible cannot be removed from the selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382				0	id	Calculating Across Multiple Sheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	id	You can refer to a range of sheets in a formula by specifying the first and last sheet of the range, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1) \</item\>sums up all A1 cells on Sheet1 through Sheet3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Creating Pivot Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148491				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; calling up and applying\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491				0	id	\<variable id=\"datapilot_createtable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_createtable.xhp\" name=\"Creating Pivot Tables\"\>Creating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	id	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Create\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Select Source\</emph\> dialog appears. Choose \<emph\>Current selection\</emph\> and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The table headings are shown as buttons in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. Drag these buttons as required and drop them into the layout areas "Page Fields", "Column Fields", "Row Fields" and "Data Fields".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	id	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id7599414				0	id	Drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the generated pivot table. The listbox can be used to filter the pivot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	id	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	id	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	id	Use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Field\</item\> dialog to select the calculations to be used for the data. To make a multiple selection, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key while clicking the desired calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	id	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	id	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	id	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialog to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	id	Exit the Pivot Table dialog by pressing OK. A \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button will now be inserted, or a page button for every data field that you dropped in the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area. The pivot table is inserted further down.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Formatting Numbers With Decimals				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145367				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;formatting decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults; number formats in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places;formatting numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers with decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;adding/deleting decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; adding/deleting decimal places in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places; adding/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	id	\<variable id=\"format_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers With Decimals\"\>Formatting Numbers With Decimals\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	id	Enter a number into the sheet, for example, 1234.5678. This number will be displayed in the default number format, with two decimal places. You will see 1234.57 when you confirm the entry. Only the display in the document will be rounded off; internally, the number retains all four decimal places after the decimal point.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	id	To format numbers with decimals:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	id	Set the cursor at the number and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> to start the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	id	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab you will see a selection of predefined number formats. In the bottom right in the dialog you will see a preview of how your current number would look if you were to give it a particular format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id3149021\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberformatincdecimals.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149021\"\>Ikon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256				0	id	If you only want to modify the number of the decimal places displayed, the easiest method is to use the \<emph\>Number Format: Add Decimal Place\</emph\> or \<emph\>Number Format: Delete Decimal Place\</emph\> icons on the Formatting Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Deactivating Automatic Changes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>deactivating; automatic changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; deactivating automatic changes in\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoInput function on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; AutoInput function of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>input support in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; input in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;cell contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell input;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;avoiding conversion to\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	id	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Deactivating Automatic Changes\"\>Deactivating Automatic Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	id	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. You can immediately undo any automatic changes with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	id	The following shows you how to deactivate and reactivate the automatic changes in $[officename] Calc:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	id	Pelengkapan angka atau teks otomatis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	id	When making an entry in a cell, $[officename] Calc automatically suggests matching input found in the same column. This function is known as \<emph\>AutoInput\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	id	To turn the AutoInput on and off, set or remove the check mark in front of \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972				0	id	Otomatis konversi ke bentuk tanggal				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	id	$[officename] Calc automatically converts certain entries to dates. For example, the entry \<emph\>1.1\</emph\> may be interpreted as January 1 of the current year, according to the locale settings of your operating system, and then displayed according to the date format applied to the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	id	To ensure that an entry is interpreted as text, add an apostrophe at the beginning of the entry. The apostrophe is not displayed in the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	id	Quotation Marks Replaced by Custom Quotes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Localized Options\</emph\> tab and unmark \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	id	Isi sel selalu diawali huruf besar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab. Unmark \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	id	Ganti kata dengan kata lain				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab. Select the word pair and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Delete\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Perkakas - Isi Sel - OtoMasukan\"\>Perkakas - Isi Sel - OtoMasukan\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Perkakas - OtoKoreksi\"\>Perkakas - Otokoreksi\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Entering Fractions 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>fractions; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; entering fractions \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;fractions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	id	\<variable id=\"fraction_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/fraction_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Fractions \"\>Entering Fractions \</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	id	You can enter a fractional number in a cell and use it for calculation:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133				0	id	Enter "0 1/5" in a cell (without the quotation marks) and press the input key. In the input line above the spreadsheet you will see the value 0.2, which is used for the calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	id	If you enter "0 1/2" AutoCorrect causes the three characters 1, / and 2 to be replaced by a single character. The same applies to 1/4 and 3/4. This replacement is defined in \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Options\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367	44			0	id	If you want to see multi-digit fractions such as "1/10", you must change the cell format to the multi-digit fraction view. Open the context menu of the cell, and choose \<emph\>Format cells. \</emph\>Select "Fraction" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, and then select "-1234 10/81". You can then enter fractions such as 12/31 or 12/32 - the fractions are, however, automatically reduced, so that in the last example you would see 3/8.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Copying Formulas				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151113				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151113				0	id	\<variable id=\"formula_copy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_copy.xhp\" name=\"Copying Formulas\"\>Copying Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	id	There are various ways to copy a formula. One suggested method is:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	id	Select the cell containing the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	id	Select the cell into which you want the formula to be copied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V. The formula will be positioned in the new cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	id	If you want to copy a formula into multiple cells, there is a quick and easy way to copy into adjacent cell areas:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	id	Select the cell containing the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	id	Position the mouse on the bottom right of the highlighted border of the cell, and continue holding down the mouse button until the pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	id	With the mouse button pressed, drag it down or to the right over all the cells into which you want to copy the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	id	When you release the mouse button, the formula will be copied into the cells and automatically adjusted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385				0	id	If you do not want values and texts to be automatically adjusted, then hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key when dragging. Formulas, however, are always adjusted accordingly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Menerapkan Banyak Operasi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\> 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	id	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	id	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulas that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	id	Select all desired sheets by holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still gray at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	id	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	id	Now when you insert values, text or formulas into the active sheet, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets. For example, data entered in cell A1 of the active sheet is automatically entered into cell A1 of any other seleted sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Updating Pivot Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; refreshing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recalculating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	id	\<variable id=\"datapilot_updatetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_updatetable.xhp\" name=\"Updating Pivot Tables\"\>Updating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	id	If the data of the source sheet has been changed, $[officename] recalculates the pivot table. To recalculate the table, choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Refresh\</emph\>. Do the same after you have imported an Excel pivot table into $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Menerapkan Saring Otomatis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>filters, see also AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoFilter function;applying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; filter values\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; filter sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drop-down menus in sheet columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>database ranges; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	id	\<variable id=\"autofilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autofilter.xhp\" name=\"Applying AutoFilter\"\>Applying AutoFilter\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	id	The \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function inserts a combo box on one or more data columns that lets you select the records (rows) to be displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	id	Select the columns you want to use AutoFilter on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>. The combo box arrows are visible in the first row of the range selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	id	Run the filter by clicking the drop-down arrow in the column heading and choosing an item.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	id	Only those rows whose contents meet the filter criteria are displayed. The other rows are filtered. You can see if rows have been filtered from the discontinuous row numbers. The column that has been used for the filter is identified by a different color for the arrow button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id9216589				0	id	When you apply an additional AutoFilter on another column of a filtered data range, then the other combo boxes list only the filtered data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	12			0	id	To display all records again, select the "all\<emph\>"\</emph\> entry in the AutoFilter combo box. If you choose "Standard\<emph\>"\</emph\>, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Standard Filter\</item\> dialog appears, allowing you to set up a standard filter. Choose "Top 10" to display the highest 10 values only. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	id	To stop using AutoFilter, reselect all cells selected in step 1 and once again choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id4303415				0	id	To assign different AutoFilters to different sheets, you must first define a database range on each sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	id	The arithmetic functions also take account of the cells that are not visible due to an applied filter. For example, a sum of an entire column will also total the values in the filtered cells. Apply the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\> function if only the cells visible after the application of a filter are to be taken into account.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040100.xhp\" name=\"Data - Filter - AutoFilter\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Melindungi Sel dari Perubahan				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>protecting;cells and sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell protection; enabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; hiding for printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; sheet protection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas;hiding\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	id	\<variable id=\"cell_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\" name=\"Melindungi Sel dari Perubahan\"\>Melindungi Sel dari Perubahan\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	id	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can protect sheets and the document as a whole. You can choose whether the cells are protected against accidental changes, whether the formulas can be viewed from within Calc, whether the cells are visible or whether the cells can be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145261				0	id	Protection can be provided by means of a password, but it does not have to be. If you have assigned a password, protection can only be removed once the correct password has been entered.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	id	Note that the cell protection for cells with the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute is only effective when you protect the whole sheet. In the default condition, every cell has the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute. Therefore you must remove the attribute selectively for those cells where the user may make changes. You then protect the whole sheet and save the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	id	These protection features are just switches to prevent accidental action. The features are not intended to provide any secure protection. For example, by exporting a sheet to another file format, a user may be able to surpass the protection features. There is only one secure protection: the password that you can apply when saving an OpenDocument file. A file that has been saved with a password can be opened only with the same password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	id	Select the cells that you want to specify the cell protection options for.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149019				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> and click the \<emph\>Cell Protection\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	id	Select the protection options that you want. All options will be applied only after you protect the sheet from the Tools menu - see below.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id31529866655				0	id	Uncheck \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to allow the user to change the currently selected cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152898	10			0	id	Select \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to prevent changes to the contents and the format of a cell. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069A				0	id	Select \<emph\>Hide formula\</emph\> to hide and to protect formulas from changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A1				0	id	Select \<emph\>Hide when printing\</emph\> to hide protected cells in the printed document. The cells are not hidden onscreen.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152872				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	id	Apply the protection options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	id	To protect the cells from being changed / viewed / printed according to your settings in the \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> dialog, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C7				0	id	To protect the structure of the document, for example the count, \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\"\>names\</link\>, and order of the sheets, from being changed, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CF				0	id	(Optional) Enter a password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	id	If you forget your password, you cannot deactivate the protection. If you only want to protect cells from accidental changes, set the sheet protection, but do not enter a password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810	13			0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	id	            \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>         				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Writing Multi-line Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; multi-line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; text breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>breaks in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multi-line text in cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	id	\<variable id=\"text_wrap\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_wrap.xhp\" name=\"Writing Multi-line Text\"\>Writing Multi-line Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	id	Pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys inserts a manual line break. This shortcut only works directly in the cell, not in the input line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	id	If you want the text to automatically break at the right border of the cell, proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	id	Select all the cells where you want the text to break at the right border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	id	In \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Wrap text automatically\</emph\> option and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sel\"\>Format - Sel\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Menyimpan dan Membuka Lembar Kerja dalam HTML				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150542				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150542				0	id	\<variable id=\"html_doc\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/html_doc.xhp\" name=\"Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\"\>Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124				0	id	Menyimpan Lembar Kerja dalam HTML				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	id	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc saves all the sheets of a Calc document together as an HTML document. At the beginning of the HTML document, a heading and a list of hyperlinks are automatically added which lead to the individual sheets within the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	id	Numbers are shown as written. In addition, in the <SDVAL> HTML tag, the exact internal number value is written so that after opening the HTML document with \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you know you have the exact values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	id	To save the current Calc document as HTML, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	id	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> list box, in the area with the other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc filters, choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	id	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149379				0	id	Membuka Lembar Kerja dalam HTML				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	id	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> offers various filters for opening HTML files, which you can select under \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Files of type\</emph\> list box:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	id	Choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	id	All \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc options are now available to you. However, not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc offers for editing can be saved in HTML format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Berkas - Buka\"\>Berkas - Buka\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Berkas - Simpan Sebagai\"\>Berkas - Simpan Sebagai\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
