helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147304				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>row headers; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column headers; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; views\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views; tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids;hiding lines in sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;headers/grid lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;table views\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147304				0	id	\<variable id=\"table_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_view.xhp\" name=\"Changing Table Views\"\>Changing Table Views\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	id	To hide column and line headers in a table:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	id	Under the menu item \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc,\</emph\> go to the \<emph\>View\</emph\> tab page. Unmark\<emph\> Column/row headers\</emph\>. Confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436				0	id	To hide grid lines:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	id	Under the menu item \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>\<emph\>,\</emph\> go to the \<emph\>View\</emph\> tab page. Unmark \<emph\>Grid lines\</emph\>. Confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows, see also cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns, see also cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	id	\<variable id=\"background\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\"\>Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id9520249				0	id	You can define a background color or use a graphic as a background for cell ranges in $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144760				0	id	Applying a Background Color to a $[officename] Calc Spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	id	Select the cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> (or \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> from the context menu).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3152938				0	id	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	id	Graphics in the Background of Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	id	Select the graphic and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153575				0	id	The graphic is inserted anchored to the current cell. You can move and scale the graphic as you want. In your context menu you can use the \<emph\>Arrange - To Background\</emph\> command to place this in the background. To select a graphic that has been placed in the background, use the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Navigator\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id51576				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/background.xhp\"\>Watermarks\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156180				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030600.xhp\" name=\"Background tab page\"\>\<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id7601245				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Formatting Spreadsheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154125				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; formatting options for selected cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies;formats\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125				0	id	\<variable id=\"format_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\" name=\"Designing Spreadsheets\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153912	13			0	id	Formatting Text in a Spreadsheet 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3144772				0	id	Select the text you want to format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268	15			0	id	Choose the desired text attributes from the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog will appear in which you can choose various text attributes on the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149899				0	id	Formatting Numbers in a Spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	id	Select the cells containing the numbers you want to format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	18			0	id	To format numbers in the default currency format or as percentages, use the icons on the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. For other formats, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You can choose from the preset formats or define your own on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153483				0	id	Formatting Borders and Backgrounds for Cells and Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733				0	id	You can assign a format to any group of cells by first selecting the cells (for multiple selection, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key when clicking), and then activating the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cell\</item\>. In this dialog, you can select attributes such as shadows and backgrounds.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	id	To apply formatting attributes to an entire sheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>. You can define headers and footers, for example, to appear on each printed page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	id	An image that you have loaded with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Background\</item\> is only visible in print or in the page preview. To display a background image on screen as well, insert the graphic image by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Picture - From File\</item\> and arrange the image behind the cells by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Arrange - To Background\</item\>. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> to select the background image.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2837916				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\"\>Number Formatting Options\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2614215				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\"\>Backgrounds for Cells\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	19xx/20xx Years				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>years; 2-digits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates; 19xx/20xx\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	id	\<variable id=\"year2000\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/year2000.xhp\" name=\"19xx/20xx Years\"\>19xx/20xx Years\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	id	The year in a date entry is often entered as two digits. Internally, the year is managed by $[officename] as four digits, so that in the calculation of the difference from 1/1/99 to 1/1/01, the result will correctly be two years.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	id	Under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\> you can define the century that is used when you enter a year with only two digits. The default is 1930 to 2029.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	id	This means that if you enter a date of 1/1/30 or higher, it will be treated internally as 1/1/1930 or higher. All lower two-digit years apply to the 20xx century. So, for example, 1/1/20 is converted into 1/1/2020.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>HTML WebQuery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; inserting in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external data; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; inserting external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>web pages; importing data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebQuery filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources; external data\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	id	\<variable id=\"webquery\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/webquery.xhp\" name=\"Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\"\>Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	id	With the help of the \<emph\>Web Page Query ($[officename] Calc)\</emph\> import filter, you can insert tables from HTML documents in a Calc spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	id	You can use the same method to insert ranges defined by name from a Calc or Microsoft Excel spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	id	The following insert methods are available:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146976				0	id	Inserting by Dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	id	Set the cell cursor at the cell where the new content will be inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Link to External Data\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\"\>External Data\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	id	Enter the URL of the HTML document or the name of the spreadsheet. Press Enter when finished. Click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open a file selection dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	id	In the large list box of the dialog, select the named ranges or tables you want to insert.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	id	You can also specify that the ranges or tables are updated every n seconds.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	id	The import filter can create names for cell ranges on the fly. As much formatting as possible is retained, while the filter intentionally does not load any images.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149021				0	id	Inserting by Navigator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	id	Open two documents: the $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in which the external data is to be inserted (target document) and the document from which the external data derives (source document).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	id	In the target document open the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	id	In the lower combo box of the Navigator select the source document. The Navigator now shows the range names and database ranges or the tables contained in the source document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148842	20			0	id	In the Navigator select the \<emph\>Insert as link\</emph\> drag mode \<image id=\"img_id3152985\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20238.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152985\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	id	Drag the desired external data from the Navigator into the target document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	id	If you have loaded an HTML document with the \<emph\>Web Page Query\</emph\> filter as the source document, you will find the tables in the Navigator, named continuously from "HTML_table1" onwards, and also two range names that have been created:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152873				0	id	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_all\</item\> - designates the entire document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149897				0	id	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_tables\</item\> - designates all HTML tables in the document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149126				0	id	Editing the external data				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3159228				0	id	Open \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\>. Here you can edit the link to the external data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154650				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External data dialog\"\>External data dialog\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Grouping Pivot Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	bm_id4195684				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function;grouping table entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping entries in pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	id	\<variable id=\"datapilot_grouping\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_grouping.xhp\"\>Grouping Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	id	The resulting pivot table can contain many different entries. By grouping the entries, you can improve the visible result.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	id	Select a cell or range of cells in the pivot table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Group\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	id	Depending on the format of the selected cells, either a new group field is added to the pivot table, or you see one of the two \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090400.xhp\"\>Grouping\</link\> dialogs, either for numeric values, or for date values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_id3328653				0	id	The pivot table must be organized in a way that grouping can be applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	id	To remove a grouping, click inside the group, then choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Ungroup\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>tables; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>freezing rows or columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrolling prevention in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; splitting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; splitting windows\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	id	\<variable id=\"line_fix\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/line_fix.xhp\" name=\"Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\"\>Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	id	If you have long rows or columns of data that extend beyond the viewable area of the sheet, you can freeze some rows or columns, which allows you to see the frozen columns or rows as you scroll through the rest of the data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	id	Select the row below, or the column to the right of the row or column that you want to be in the frozen region. All rows above, or all columns to the left of the selection are frozen.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	id	To freeze both horizontally and vertically, select the \<emph\>cell\</emph\> that is below the row and to the right of the column that you want to freeze.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	5			0	id	To deactivate, choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze \</emph\>again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	id	If the area defined is to be scrollable, apply the \<emph\>Window - Split\</emph\> command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	id	If you want to print a certain row on all pages of a document, choose \<emph\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Freeze\"\>Window - Freeze\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Split\"\>Window - Split\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Cells in Currency Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156329				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>currency formats; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>international currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; currency formats in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies; default currencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329				0	id	\<variable id=\"currency_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/currency_format.xhp\" name=\"Cells in Currency Format\"\>Cells in Currency Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	id	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can give numbers any currency format. When you click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Currency\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150791\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_currencyfield.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150791\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar to format a number, the cell is given the default currency format set under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	id	Exchanging of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc documents can lead to misunderstandings, if your \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc document is loaded by a user who uses a different default currency format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	id	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can define that a number that you have formatted as "1,234.50 €", still remains in euros in another country and does not become dollars.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	id	You can change the currency format in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format Cells\</item\> dialog (choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</item\> tab) by two country settings. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\> combo box select the basic setting for decimal and thousands separators. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box you can select the currency symbol and its position.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	id	For example, if the language is set to "Default" and you are using a german locale setting, the currency format will be "1.234,00 €". A point is used before the thousand digits and a comma before the decimal places. If you now select the subordinate currency format "$ English (US)" from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box , you will get the following format: "$ 1.234,00". As you can see, the separators have remained the same. Only the currency symbol has been changed and converted, but the underlying format of the notation remains the same as in the locale setting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	id	If, under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\>, you convert the cells to "English (US)", the English-language locale setting is also transferred and the default currency format is now "$ 1,234.00".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Entering Matrix Formulas				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153969				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>matrices; entering matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969				0	id	\<variable id=\"matrixformula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/matrixformula.xhp\" name=\"Entering Matrix Formulas\"\>Entering Matrix Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	id	The following is an example of how you can enter a matrix formula, without going into the details of matrix functions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	id	Assume you have entered 10 numbers in Columns A and B (A1:A10 and B1:B10), and would like to calculate the sum of each row in Column C.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	id	Using the mouse, select the range C1:C10, in which the results are to be displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	id	Press F2, or click in the input line of the Formula bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	id	Enter an equal sign (=).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	id	Select the range A1:A10, which contains the first values for the sum formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	id	Press the (+) key from the numerical keypad.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	id	Select the numbers in the second column in cells B1:B10.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	id	End the input with the matrix key combination: Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	id	The matrix area is automatically protected against modifications, such as deleting rows or columns. It is, however, possible to edit any formatting, such as the cell background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Formatting Numbers as Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;entering as text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text formats; for numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell formats; text/numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	id	\<variable id=\"text_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers as Text\"\>Formatting Numbers as Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	id	You can format numbers as text in $[officename] Calc. Open the context menu of a cell or range of cells and choose \<emph\>Format Cells - Numbers\</emph\>, then select "Text" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list. Any numbers subsequently entered into the formatted range are interpreted as text. The display of these "numbers" is left-justified, just as with other text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	id	If you have already entered normal numbers in cells and have afterwards changed the format of the cells to "Text", the numbers will remain normal numbers. They will not be converted. Only numbers entered afterwards, or numbers which are then edited, will become text numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	id	If you decide to enter a number directly as text, enter an apostrophe (') first. For example, for years in column headings, you can enter '1999, '2000 and '2001. The apostrophe is not visible in the cell, it only indicates that the entry is to be recognized as a text. This is useful if, for example, you enter a telephone number or postal code that begins with a zero (0), because a zero (0) at the start of a sequence of digits is removed in normal number formats.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Applying Goal Seek				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>goal seeking;example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>equations in goal seek\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variables in equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;calculating equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;goal seek\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	id	\<variable id=\"goalseek\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/goalseek.xhp\" name=\"Applying Goal Seek\"\>Applying Goal Seek\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	id	With the help of Goal Seek you can calculate a value that, as part of a formula, leads to the result you specify for the formula. You thus define the formula with several fixed values and one variable value and the result of the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153966				0	id	Goal Seek Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150871				0	id	To calculate annual interest (I), create a table with the values for the capital (C), number of years (n), and interest rate (i). The formula is:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	id	I = C * n* i				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	id	Let us assume that the interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> of 7.5% and the number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\> (1) will remain constant. However, you want to know how much the investment capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would have to be modified in order to attain a particular return \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>. For this example, calculate how much capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would be required if you want an annual return of $15,000.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	id	Enter each of the values for Capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> (an arbitrary value like \<item type=\"literal\"\>$100,000\</item\>), number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n \</item\>(\<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>), and interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> (\<item type=\"literal\"\>7.5%\</item\>) in one cell each. Enter the formula to calculate the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\> in another cell. Instead of \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\"\>reference to the cell\</link\> with the corresponding value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	id	Place the cursor in the cell containing the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>, and choose \<emph\>Tools - Goal Seek\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Goal Seek\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	id	The correct cell is already entered in the field \<emph\>Formula Cell\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	id	Place the cursor in the field \<emph\>Variable Cell\</emph\>. In the sheet, click in the cell that contains the value to be changed, in this example it is the cell with the capital value \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	id	Enter the expected result of the formula in the \<emph\>Target Value\</emph\> text box. In this example, the value is 15,000. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	id	A dialog appears informing you that the Goal Seek was successful. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to enter the result in the cell with the variable value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Goal Seek\"\>Goal Seek\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Sorting Data 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150767				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; sorting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sorting; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data;sorting in databases\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	id	\<variable id=\"database_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_sort.xhp\" name=\"Sorting Database Ranges\"\>Sorting Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3145751				0	id	Click in a database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121549				0	id	If you select a range of cells, only these cells will get sorted. If you just click one cell without selecting, then the whole database range will get sorted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10635				0	id	Pilih \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Validitas\</item\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121547				0	id	The range of cells that will get sorted is shown in inverted colors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	id	Select the sort options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063D				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1846980				0	id	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Defining_a_Data_Range\"\>Wiki page about defining a data range\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Referencing a Cell in Another Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>sheet references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; to cells in other sheets/documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; operating in another document\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents;references\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	id	\<variable id=\"cellreferences\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Other Sheets\"\>Referencing Other Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9663075				0	id	In a sheet cell you can show a reference to a cell in another sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id1879329				0	id	In the same way, a reference can also be made to a cell from another document provided that this document has already been saved as a file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id7122409				0	id	To Reference a Cell in the Same Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id2078005				0	id	Open a new, empty spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id4943693				0	id	By way of example, enter the following formula in cell A1 of Sheet1:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9064302				0	id	               \<item type=\"literal\"\>=Sheet2.A1\</item\>            				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7609790				0	id	Click the \<emph\>Sheet 2\</emph\> tab at the bottom of the spreadsheet. Set the cursor in cell A1 there and enter text or a number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	id	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also change.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id9209570				0	id	To Reference a Cell in Another Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell where you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	id	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	id	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	id	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	id	Confirm the formula by clicking the green check mark.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	id	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	id	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>addressing; relative and absolute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; absolute/relative\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute addresses in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative addresses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute references in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; to cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; references\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	id	\<variable id=\"relativ_absolut_ref\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\" name=\"Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\"\>Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163712				0	id	Relative Addressing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	id	The cell in column A, row 1 is addressed as A1. You can address a range of adjacent cells by first entering the coordinates of the upper left cell of the area, then a colon followed by the coordinates of the lower right cell. For example, the square formed by the first four cells in the upper left corner is addressed as A1:B2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	id	By addressing an area in this way, you are making a relative reference to A1:B2. Relative here means that the reference to this area will be adjusted automatically when you copy the formulas.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	id	Absolute Addressing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	id	Absolute references are the opposite of relative addressing. A dollar sign is placed before each letter and number in an absolute reference, for example, $A$1:$B$2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	id	$[officename] can convert the current reference, in which the cursor is positioned in the input line, from relative to absolute and vice versa by pressing Shift +F4. If you start with a relative address such as A1, the first time you press this key combination, both row and column are set to absolute references ($A$1). The second time, only the row (A$1), and the third time, only the column ($A1). If you press the key combination once more, both column and row references are switched back to relative (A1)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	id	$[officename] Calc shows the references to a formula. If, for example you click the formula =SUM(A1:C5;D15:D24) in a cell, the two referenced areas in the sheet will be highlighted in color. For example, the formula component "A1:C5" may be in blue and the cell range in question bordered in the same shade of blue. The next formula component "D15:D24" can be marked in red in the same way.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	id	When to Use Relative and Absolute References				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	id	What distinguishes a relative reference? Assume you want to calculate in cell E1 the sum of the cells in range A1:B2. The formula to enter into E1 would be: =SUM(A1:B2). If you later decide to insert a new column in front of column A, the elements you want to add would then be in B1:C2 and the formula would be in F1, not in E1. After inserting the new column, you would therefore have to check and correct all formulas in the sheet, and possibly in other sheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	id	Fortunately, $[officename] does this work for you. After having inserted a new column A, the formula =SUM(A1:B2) will be automatically updated to =SUM(B1:C2). Row numbers will also be automatically adjusted when a new row 1 is inserted. Absolute and relative references are always adjusted in $[officename] Calc whenever the referenced area is moved. But be careful if you are copying a formula since in that case only the relative references will be adjusted, not the absolute references.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791				0	id	Absolute references are used when a calculation refers to one specific cell in your sheet. If a formula that refers to exactly this cell is copied relatively to a cell below the original cell, the reference will also be moved down if you did not define the cell coordinates as absolute.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	id	Aside from when new rows and columns are inserted, references can also change when an existing formula referring to particular cells is copied to another area of the sheet. Assume you entered the formula =SUM(A1:A9) in row 10. If you want to calculate the sum for the adjacent column to the right, simply copy this formula to the cell to the right. The copy of the formula in column B will be automatically adjusted to =SUM(B1:B9).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Finding and Replacing in Calc				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulas/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	id	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	id	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulas, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	id	The Find & Replace dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	id	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	id	To find formulas or values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	id	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialog either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	id	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	id	Select "Formulas" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	id	With "Formulas" you will find all parts of the formulas. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	id	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	id	Cell contents can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	id	Finding text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	id	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	id	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	id	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	id	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialog. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	id	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	id	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	id	The Navigator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	id	Choose \<emph\>View - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	id	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	id	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Kalkulasi dalam Pengolah Angka				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; calculating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; calculating\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	id	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Kalkulasi dalam Pengolah Angka\"\>Kalkulasi dalam Pengolah Angka\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	id	The following is an example of a calculation in $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	id	Click in a cell, and type a number				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN10656				0	id	Press Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065D				0	id	The cursor moves down to the next cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	id	Enter another number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066F				0	id	Press the Tab key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN10676				0	id	The cursor moves to the right into the next cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	id	Type in a formula, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A3 * A4 / 100.\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068B				0	id	 Press Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	id	The result of the formula appears in the cell. If you want, you can edit the formula in the input line of the Formula bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155378				0	id	When you edit a formula, the new result is calculated automatically.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Displaying Formulas or Values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153195				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; displaying in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values; displaying in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; displaying formulas/values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>results display vs. formulas display\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; formulas instead of results\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153195				0	id	\<variable id=\"formula_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_value.xhp\" name=\"Displaying Formulas or Values\"\>Displaying Formulas or Values\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	id	If you want to display the formulas in the cells, for example in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	id	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	id	In the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> box. Click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	id	If you want to view the calculation results instead of the formula, do not mark the Formulas box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Defining Number of Pages for Printing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153194				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; spreadsheet preview\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>previews;page breaks for printing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194				0	id	\<variable id=\"print_exact\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_exact.xhp\" name=\"Defining Number of Pages for Printing\"\>Defining Number of Pages for Printing\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	id	If a sheet is too large for a single printed page, $[officename] Calc will print the current sheet evenly divided over several pages. Since the automatic page break does not always take place in the optimal position, you can define the page distribution yourself.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	id	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	id	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	id	You will see the automatic distribution of the sheet across the print pages. The automatically created print ranges are indicated by dark blue lines, and the user-defined ones by light blue lines. The page breaks (line breaks and column breaks) are marked as black lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	id	You can move the blue lines with the mouse. You will find further options in the Context menu, including adding an additional print range, removing the scaling and inserting additional manual line and column breaks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Entering a Number with Leading Zeros				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147560				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>zero values; entering leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>integers with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; changing text/number\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; changing to numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text with leading zeros, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560				0	id	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	id	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	id	Enter the number as text. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, \<item type=\"input\"\>'0987\</item\>). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as text. Because it is in text format, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	id	Format a cell with a number format such as \<item type=\"input\"\>\\0000\</item\>. This format can be assigned in the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> field under the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab, and defines the cell display as "always put a zero first and then the integer, having at least three places, and filled with zeros at the left if less than three digits".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	id	If you want to apply a numerical format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	id	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	id	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>^[0-9]\</item\>               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	id	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>&\</item\>               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	id	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	id	Check \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	id	Click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>               				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Deleting Pivot Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; deleting tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	id	\<variable id=\"datapilot_deletetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_deletetable.xhp\" name=\"Deleting Pivot Tables\"\>Deleting Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	id	In order to delete a pivot table, click any cell in the pivot table, then choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> in the context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Mencabut Proteksi terhadap Sel				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153252				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>cell protection; unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting; unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252	14			0	id	\<variable id=\"cell_unprotect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_unprotect.xhp\" name=\"Mencabut Proteksi terhadap Sel\"\>Mencabut Proteksi terhadap Sel\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	id	Click the sheet for which you want to cancel the protection.				20181231 09:50:43
