helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541				0	id	\<variable id=\"database_filter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_filter.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Cell Ranges\"\>Filtering Cell Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	id	You can use several filters to filter cell ranges in spreadsheets. A standard filter uses the options that you specify to filter the data. An AutoFilter filters data according to a specific value or string. An advanced filter uses filter criteria from specified cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	id	To Apply a Standard Filter to a Cell Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	id	Click in a cell range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10693				0	id	Pilih \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Penyaring - Penyaring Standar\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	id	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog, specify the filter options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A5				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	id	The records that match the filter options that you specified are shown.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	id	To Apply an AutoFilter to a Cell Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	id	Click in a cell range or a database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id9303872				0	id	If you want to apply multiple AutoFilters to the same sheet, you must first define database ranges, then apply the AutoFilters to the database ranges.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	id	Pilih \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Penyaring - Buang Penyaring\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DB				0	id	An arrow button is added to the head of each column in the database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	id	Click the arrow button in the column that contains the value or string that you want to set as the filter criteria.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	id	Select the value or string that you want to use as the filter criteria.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	id	The records that match the filter criteria that you selected are shown.				20181231 09:50:43
