helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; preventing data overwriting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>output ranges of pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663				0	id	\<variable id=\"datapilot_tipps\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_tipps.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\"\>Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	id	Click the button \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. The dialog will be extended.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	id	You can select a named range in which the pivot table is to be created, from the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. If the results range does not have a name, enter the coordinates of the upper left cell of the range into the field to the right of the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. You can also click on the appropriate cell to have the coordinates entered accordingly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	id	If you mark the \<emph\>Ignore empty rows\</emph\> check box, they will not be taken into account when the pivot table is created.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	id	If the \<emph\>Identify categories\</emph\> check box is marked, the categories will be identified by their headings and assigned accordingly when the pivot table is created.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Navigating Through Sheets Tabs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; showing multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769	4			0	id	\<variable id=\"multi_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multi_tables.xhp\" name=\"Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\"\>Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	id	By default $[officename] displays three sheets "Sheet1" to "Sheet3", in each new spreadsheet. You can switch between sheets in a spreadsheet using the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	id	 \<image id=\"img_id4829822\" src=\"res/helpimg/sheettabs.png\" width=\"3.3335inch\" height=\"0.7638inch\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4829822\"\>Sheet Tabs\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id3156441\" src=\"res/helpimg/calcnav.png\" width=\"1.667cm\" height=\"0.37cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156441\"\>Ikon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	id	Use the navigation buttons to display all the sheets belonging to your document. Clicking the button on the far left or the far right displays, respectively, the first or last sheet tab. The middle buttons allow the user to scroll forward and backward through all sheet tabs. To display the sheet itself click on the sheet tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	id	If there is insufficient space to display all the sheet tabs, you can increase it by pointing to the separator between the scrollbar and the sheet tabs, pressing the mouse button and, keeping the mouse button pressed, dragging to the right. In doing so you will be sharing the available space between the sheet tabs and horizontal scrollbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Memasukkan Nilai				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>values; inserting in multiple cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;values\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;selecting for data entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>areas, see also cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3405255				0	id	\<variable id=\"cell_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_enter.xhp\"\>Memasukkan Nilai\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7147129				0	id	Calc can simplify entering data and values into multiple cells. You can change some settings to conform to your preferences.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id5621509				0	id	To Enter Values Into a Range of Cells Manually				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8200018				0	id	There are two features that assist you when you enter a block of data manually.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id1867427				0	id	Area Detection for New Rows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7908871				0	id	In the row below a heading row, you can advance from one cell to the next with the Tab key. After you enter the value into the last cell in the current row, press Enter. Calc positions the cursor below the first cell of the current block.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6196783				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id6473586\" src=\"res/helpimg/area1.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6473586\"\>area detection\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8118839				0	id	In row 3, press Tab to advance from cell B3 to C3, D3, and E3. Then press Enter to advance to B4.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3583788				0	id	Seleksi area				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id2011780				0	id	Use drag-and-drop to select the area where you want to input values. But start dragging from the last cell of the area and release the mouse button when you have selected the first cell. Now you can start to input values. Always press the Tab key to advance to the next cell. You will not leave the selected area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7044282				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id2811365\" src=\"res/helpimg/area2.png\" width=\"6.4437inch\" height=\"2.1252inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2811365\"\>seleksi area\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3232520				0	id	Select the area from E7 to B3. Now B3 is waiting for your input. Press Tab to advance to the next cell within the selected area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id8950163				0	id	To Enter Values to a Range of Cells Automatically				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id633869				0	id	See \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Rotating Tables (Transposing)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>tables; transposing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transposing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inverting tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>swapping tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; swap with rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; swapping with columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; rotating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rotating; tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	id	\<variable id=\"table_rotate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_rotate.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Tables (Transposing)\"\>Rotating Tables (Transposing)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	id	In $[officename] Calc, there is a way to "rotate" a spreadsheet so that rows become columns and columns become rows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	id	Select the cell range that you want to transpose.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	id	Click the cell that is to be the top left cell in the result.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	id	In the dialog, mark \<emph\>Paste all\</emph\> and \<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	id	If you now click OK the columns and rows are transposed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\" name=\"Paste Special\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Printing Sheets in Landscape Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet selections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing in landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing; landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape printing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	id	\<variable id=\"print_landscape\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_landscape.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\"\>Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257				0	id	In order to print a sheet you have a number of interactive options available under \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>. Drag the delimiter lines to define the range of printed cells on each page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	id	To print in landscape format, proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	id	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089	5			0	id	The command is not visible if the sheet has been opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	id	Select the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab. Select the \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\> paper format and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150885				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288				0	id	Depending on the printer driver and the operating system, it may be necessary to click the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button and to change your printer to landscape format there.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404	9			0	id	In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>dialog in the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the contents to be printed:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	10			0	id	               \<emph\>All sheets\</emph\> - All sheets will be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	12			0	id	               \<emph\>Selected sheets\</emph\> - Only the selected sheets will be printed. All sheets whose names (at the bottom on the sheet tabs) are selected will be printed. By pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while clicking a sheet name you can change this selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3764763				0	id	               \<emph\>Selected cells\</emph\> - All selected cells are printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id5538804				0	id	From all the paper pages that result from the above selection, you can select the range of paper pages to be printed:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id14343				0	id	               \<emph\>All pages\</emph\> - Print all resulting pages.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699	11			0	id	               \<emph\>Pages\</emph\> - Enter the pages to be printed. The pages will also be numbered from the first sheet onwards. If you see in the Page Break Preview that Sheet1 will be printed on 4 pages and you want to print the first two pages of Sheet2, enter 5-6 here.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3145076				0	id	If under \<emph\>Format - Print ranges\</emph\> you have defined one or more print ranges, only the contents of these print ranges will be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id8254646				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155686				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; moving cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; moving by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;moving by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;cells by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cells, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id986358				0	id	\<variable id=\"move_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/move_dragdrop.xhp\"\>Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	id	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	id	When you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	id	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	id	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	id	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	id	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	id	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	id	In both modes, you can hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	id	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	id	Hasil				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	id	No key				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	id	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	id	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	id	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9518723				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	id	Cells are moved and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells are emptied, except if you move within the same rows on the same sheet. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4021423				0	id	If you move within the same rows on the same sheet, the cells in the target area shift to the right, and then the whole row shifts to fill the source area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>keys				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2785119				0	id	Cells are copied and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id584124				0	id	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5590990				0	id	Links to the source cells are inserted and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Importing and Exporting dBASE Files 				20181231 09:50:43
