helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	id	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBASE Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	id	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	id	To Import a dBASE File Into a Spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	id	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	id	The \<emph\>Import dBASE files\</emph\> dialog opens.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	id	The dBASE file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	id	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBASE file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBASE database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	id	To Import a dBASE File Into a Database Table				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	id	A %PRODUCTNAME Base database table is actually a link to an existing database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10796				0	id	Pilih \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Berkas - Baru - Basis Data\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	id	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialog, enter a name for the database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10792				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	id	In the \<emph\>Database type \</emph\>box of the \<emph\>Database Properties\</emph\> dialog, select "dBASE".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B6				0	id	Locate the directory that contains the dBASE file, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F1				0	id	To Save a Spreadsheet as a dBASE File				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10800				0	id	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> box, select "dBASE file".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	id	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, type a name for the dBASE file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10801				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10808				0	id	Only the data on the current sheet is exported.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154686				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; referencing cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; referencing by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references;inserting by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;references, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154686				0	id	\<variable id=\"cellreference_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreference_dragdrop.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop\"\>Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	id	With the help of the Navigator you can reference cells from one sheet to another sheet in the same document or in a different document. The cells can be inserted as a copy, link, or hyperlink. The range to be inserted must be defined with a name in the original file so that it can be inserted in the target file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	id	Open the document that contains the source cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	id	To set the source range as the range, select the cells and choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. Save the source document, and do not close it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	id	Open the sheet in which you want to insert something.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154732				0	id	Open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>. In the lower box of the Navigator select the source file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	id	In the Navigator, the source file object appears under "Range names".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	id	Using the \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon in Navigator, choose whether you want the reference to be a hyperlink, link, or copy.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	id	Click the name under "Range names" in the Navigator, and drag into the cell of the current sheet where you want to insert the reference.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	id	This method can also be used to insert a range from another sheet of the same document into the current sheet. Select the active document as source in step 4 above.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Handling of Empty Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146799				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>kode kesalahan;daftar dari\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id1502121				0	id	\<variable id=\"empty_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/05/empty_cells.xhp\"\>Handling of Empty Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	id	In older versions of the software, empty cells were forced to numeric 0 in some contexts and to empty string in others, except in direct comparison where =A1=0 and =A1="" both resulted in TRUE if A1 was empty. Emptiness now is inherited until used, so both =VLOOKUP(...)=0 and =VLOOKUP(...)="" give TRUE if the lookup resulted in an empty cell being returned. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2733542				0	id	A simple reference to an empty cell is still displayed as numeric 0 but is not necessarily of type numeric anymore, so also comparisons with the referencing cell work as expected. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4238715				0	id	For the following examples, A1 contains a number, B1 is empty, C1 contains the reference to B1:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8277230				0	id	A1: 1 B1: <empty> C1: =B1 (displays 0)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4086428				0	id	=B1=0 => TRUE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9024628				0	id	=B1="" => TRUE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3067110				0	id	=C1=0 => TRUE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8841822				0	id	=C1="" => TRUE (previously was FALSE)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4077578				0	id	=ISNUMBER(B1) => FALSE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9094515				0	id	=ISNUMBER(C1) => FALSE (previously was TRUE)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id396740				0	id	=ISNUMBER(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;2)) => FALSE (B1)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3859675				0	id	=ISNUMBER(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;3)) => FALSE (C1, previously was TRUE)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id402233				0	id	=ISTEXT(B1) => FALSE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1623889				0	id	=ISTEXT(C1) => FALSE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id7781914				0	id	=ISTEXT(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;2)) => FALSE (B1, previously was TRUE)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id300912				0	id	=ISTEXT(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;3)) => FALSE (C1)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9534592				0	id	=ISBLANK(B1) => TRUE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4969328				0	id	=ISBLANK(C1) => FALSE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9635914				0	id	=ISBLANK(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;2)) => TRUE (B1, previously was FALSE)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2476577				0	id	=ISBLANK(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;3)) => FALSE (C1)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4217047				0	id	Note that Microsoft Excel behaves different and always returns a number as the result of a reference to an empty cell or a formula cell with the result of an empty cell. For example:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2629474				0	id	A1: <empty>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8069704				0	id	B1: =A1 => displays 0, but is just a reference to an empty cell				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4524674				0	id	=ISNUMBER(A1) => FALSE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4396801				0	id	=ISTEXT(A1) => FALSE				20181231 09:50:43
