helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3151376				0	id	\<emph\>Date1\</emph\> is the start date, \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is the end date. If \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is an earlier date than \<emph\>Date1\</emph\> the result is a negative number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151001				0	id	Contoh				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3159101				0	id	=DAYS("2010-01-01"; NOW()) returns the number of days from today until January 1, 2010.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days.xhp	0	help	par_id3163720				0	id	=DAYS("1990-10-10";"1980-10-10") returns 3652 days.				20181231 09:50:43
