helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	id	Contoh				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154633				0	id	What is the probability with ten throws of the dice, that a six will come up exactly twice? The probability of a six (or any other number) is 1/6. The following formula combines these factors:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149393	41			0	id	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=B(10;1/6;2)\</item\> returns a probability of 29%.				20181231 09:50:43
