helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3938413				0	id	\<emph\>Year\</emph\> is an integer between 1583 and 9956 or 0 and 99. You can also calculate other holidays by simple addition with this date.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	id	Easter Monday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) + 1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3147521				0	id	Good Friday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) - 2				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3146072				0	id	Pentecost Sunday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) + 49				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149553				0	id	Pentecost Monday = EASTERSUNDAY(Year) + 50				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155120				0	id	Contoh				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154472				0	id	=EASTERSUNDAY(2000) returns 2000-04-23.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940				0	id	EASTERSUNDAY(2000)+49 returns the internal serial number 36688. The result is 2000-06-11. Format the serial date number as a date, for example in the format YYYY-MM-DD.				20181231 09:50:43
