helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148754K1				0	id	AVERAGEIF				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138K1				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTB\"\>Average the values of cells in a range that meet a criteria.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153326K1				0	id	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734K1				0	id	AVERAGEIF( Reference R ; Criterion C [ ; Reference A ] )				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260K1				0	id	 If reference A is omitted, averages the values of cells in the reference range R that meet the Criterion C. If reference A is given, averages the values of cells of a range that is constructed using the top left cell of reference A and applying the dimensions, shape and size, of reference R.  Does not accept constant values as reference parameters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145139K1				0	id	If no cell in range R matches the Criterion C, an Error is returned. If no Numbers are in the range to be averaged, an Error is returned.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504K1				0	id	Examples				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864K1				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGEIF(A1:A50;">"0)\</item\>will return the average of A1:A50 of all positive values in the range.				20181231 09:50:43
