helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148742				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060103.xhp\" name=\"Back to Financial Functions Part One\"\>Back to Financial Functions Part One\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151341				0	id	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060118.xhp\" name=\"Maju ke Fungsi Keuangan Bagian Tiga\"\>Fungsi keuangan Bagian Tiga\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150026				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>fungsi UPPER\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150026				0	id	PPMT				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146942				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KAPZ\"\>Returns for a given period the payment on the principal for an investment that is based on periodic and constant payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150459				0	id	Sintaksis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146878				0	id	PV(Ongkos; NPER; PMT; FV; Jenis)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151228				0	id	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148887				0	id	\<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the amortizement period. P = 1 for the first and P = NPer for the last period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148436				0	id	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods during which annuity is paid.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153035				0	id	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present value in the sequence of payments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474				0	id	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the desired (future) value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3144744				0	id	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) defines the due date. F = 1 for payment at the beginning of a period and F = 0 for payment at the end of a period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067C				0	id	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148582				0	id	Contoh				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154811				0	id	How high is the periodic monthly payment at an annual interest rate of 8.75% over a period of 3 years? The cash value is 5,000 currency units and is always paid at the beginning of a period. The future value is 8,000 currency units.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149246				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PPMT(8.75%/12;1;36;5000;8000;1)\</item\> = -350.99 currency units.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146139				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; total amortizement rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>total amortizement rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>amortization installment\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>repayment installment\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>CUMPRINC function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	id	CUMPRINC				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150140				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUMKAPITAL\"\>Returns the cumulative interest paid for an investment period with a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149188				0	id	Sintaksis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148733				0	id	PV(Ongkos; NPER; PMT; FV; Jenis)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864				0	id	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3166052				0	id	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the payment period with the total number of periods. NPER can also be a non-integer value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150007				0	id	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the current value in the sequence of payments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153112				0	id	\<emph\>S\</emph\> is the first period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146847				0	id	\<emph\>E\</emph\> is the last period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145167				0	id	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the due date of the payment at the beginning or end of each period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154502				0	id	Contoh				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153570				0	id	What are the payoff amounts if the yearly interest rate is 5.5% for 36 months? The cash value is 15,000 currency units. The payoff amount is calculated between the 10th and 18th period. The due date is at the end of the period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149884				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CUMPRINC(5.5%/12;36;15000;10;18;0)\</item\> = -3669.74 currency units. The payoff amount between the 10th and 18th period is 3669.74 currency units.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150019				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>fungsi CUMPRINC_ADD\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150019				0	id	CUMPRINC_ADD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145246				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_CUMPRINC\"\> Calculates the cumulative redemption of a loan in a period.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153047				0	id	Sintaksis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3157970				0	id	CUMPRINC_ADD(Rate; NPer; PV; StartPeriod; EndPeriod; Type)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145302				0	id	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the interest rate for each period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017				0	id	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of payment periods. The rate and NPER must refer to the same unit, and thus both be calculated annually or monthly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	id	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the current value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145352				0	id	\<emph\>StartPeriod\</emph\> is the first payment period for the calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3157986				0	id	\<emph\>EndPeriod\</emph\> is the last payment period for the calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150570				0	id	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the maturity of a payment at the end of each period (Type = 0) or at the start of the period (Type = 1).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150269				0	id	Contoh				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	id	The following mortgage loan is taken out on a house:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150661				0	id	Rate: 9.00 per cent per annum (9% / 12 = 0.0075), Duration: 30 years (payment periods = 30 * 12 = 360), NPV: 125000 currency units.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155512				0	id	How much will you repay in the second year of the mortgage (thus from periods 13 to 24)?				20181231 09:50:43
