helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148399				0	id	MIRR(Values; Investment; ReinvestRate)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	id	\<emph\>Values\</emph\> corresponds to the array or the cell reference for cells whose content corresponds to the payments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149998				0	id	\<emph\>Investment\</emph\> is the rate of interest of the investments (the negative values of the array)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3159408				0	id	\<emph\>ReinvestRate\</emph\>:the rate of interest of the reinvestment (the positive values of the array)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154714				0	id	Contoh				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147352				0	id	Assuming a cell content of A1 = \<item type=\"input\"\>-5\</item\>, A2 = \<item type=\"input\"\>10\</item\>, A3 = \<item type=\"input\"\>15\</item\>, and A4 = \<item type=\"input\"\>8\</item\>, and an investment value of 0.5 and a reinvestment value of 0.1, the result is 94.16%.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149323				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>YIELD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rates of return;securities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>yields, see also rates of return\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
