helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158276				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_REST\"\>Returns the remainder when one integer is divided by another.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158294				0	id	Sintaksis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158308				0	id	MOD(Dividend; Divisor)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158321				0	id	 For integer arguments this function returns Dividend modulo Divisor, that is the remainder when \<emph\>Dividend\</emph\> is divided by \<emph\>Divisor\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158341				0	id	This function is implemented as \<item type=\"literal\"\>Dividend - Divisor * INT(Dividend/Divisor)\</item\> , and this formula gives the result if the arguments are not integer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158361				0	id	Contoh				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158374				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MOD(22;3)\</item\> returns 1, the remainder when 22 is divided by 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1278420				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MOD(11.25;2.5)\</item\> returns 1.25.				20181231 09:50:43
