helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146020				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number down, toward zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146037				0	id	Sintaksis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146051				0	id	ROUNDDOWN(Number; Count)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146064				0	id	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded down (towards zero) to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds down to an integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds down to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	id	This function rounds towards zero. See ROUNDUP and ROUND for alternatives.				20181231 09:50:43
