helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164884				0	id	RAND()				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5092318				0	id	This function produces a new random number each time Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F9.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9312417				0	id	To generate random numbers which never recalculate, copy cells each containing =RAND(), and use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste Special\</item\> (with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paste All\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formulas\</item\> not marked and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> marked).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id9089022				0	id	Contoh				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9569078				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=RAND()\</item\> returns a random number between 0 and 1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164897				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>fungsi DCOUNT\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>menghitung baris;dengan nilai numerik\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164897				0	id	COUNTIF				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWENN\"\>Returns the number of cells that meet with certain criteria within a cell range.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164953				0	id	Sintaksis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967				0	id	COUNTIF(jangkauan; kriteria)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980				0	id	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000				0	id	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a character string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter a search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. b.* for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165037				0	id	Contoh				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166505				0	id	A1:A10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2009\</item\>. Cell B1 contains the number \<item type=\"input\"\>2006\</item\>. In cell B2, you enter a formula:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3581652				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;2006)\</item\> - this returns 1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id708639				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;B1)\</item\> - this returns 1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;">=2006") \</item\>- this returns 4				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<"&B1)\</item\> - when B1 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>2006\</item\>, this returns 6				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id166020				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;C2)\</item\> where cell C2 contains the text \<item type=\"input\"\>>2006\</item\> counts the number of cells in the range A1:A10 which are >2006 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	id	To count only negative numbers: \<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<0")\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164897K				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTIFS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting;specified cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164897K				0	id	COUNTIFS				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926K				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWNRNG\"\>Count the number of cells that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164953K				0	id	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967K				0	id	COUNTIFS( Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980K				0	id	\<emph\>Reference R1\</emph\> is the  range to which the \<emph\>Criterion C1\</emph\>applies. \<emph\>Reference R2\</emph\> is the  range to which the \<emph\>Criterion C2\</emph\>applies, and so on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000K				0	id	All \<emph\>Reference \</emph\> ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned. \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a character string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter a search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. b.* for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165037K				0	id	Examples:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166505K				0	id	A1:A10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2009\</item\>. B1:B10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2007\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2016\</item\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3581652K				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIFS(A1:A10;2006;B1:B10;2014)\</item\> - this returns 2				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225K				0	id	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIFS(A1:A10;">=2006";B1:B10;">=2006") \</item\>- this returns 14				20181231 09:50:43
