helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id655232				0	id	\<variable id=\"text2columns\"\>Opens the Text to Columns dialog, where you enter settings to expand the contents of selected cells to multiple cells. \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	hd_id9599597				0	id	To expand cell contents to multiple cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id2021546				0	id	You can expand cells that contain comma separated values (CSV) into multiple cells in the same row. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\text2columns.xhp	0	help	par_id2623981				0	id	For example, cell A1 contains the comma separated values \<item type=\"literal\"\>1,2,3,4\</item\>, and cell A2 contains the text \<item type=\"literal\"\>A,B,C,D\</item\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
