helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154636				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VDB\"\>Returns the depreciation of an asset for a specified or partial period using a variable declining balance method.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155519				0	id	Sintaksis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149025				0	id	VDB(Cost; Salvage; Life; S; End; Factor; Type)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150692				0	id	\<emph\>Cost\</emph\> is the initial value of an asset.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155369				0	id	\<emph\>Salvage\</emph\> is the value of an asset at the end of the depreciation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154954				0	id	\<emph\>Life\</emph\> is the depreciation duration of the asset.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152817				0	id	\<emph\>S\</emph\> is the start of the depreciation. A must be entered in the same date unit as the duration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221				0	id	\<emph\>End\</emph\> is the end of the depreciation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147536				0	id	\<emph\>Factor\</emph\> (optional) is the depreciation factor. Factor = 2 is double rate depreciation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154865	232			0	id	\<emph\>Type \</emph\>is an optional parameter. Type = 1 means a switch to linear depreciation. In Type = 0 no switch is made.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0D				0	id	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
