helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154901				0	id	\<emph\>P\</emph\> is the number of periods needed for calculating the interest rate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	id	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present (current) value. The cash value is the deposit of cash or the current cash value of an allowance in kind. As a deposit value a positive value must be entered; the deposit must not be 0 or <0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149771				0	id	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> determines what is desired as the cash value of the deposit.				20181231 09:50:43
