helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916				0	id	\<variable id=\"removing_line_breaks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/removing_line_breaks.xhp\"\>Removing Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	id	Use the AutoCorrect feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	id	This AutoCorrect feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138	5			0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>               \<emph\>.\</emph\>            				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	id	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	id	Select the text containing the line breaks that you want to remove.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Apply Style\</item\> box on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar, choose “Default”.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - Apply\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147684				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>captions; adding chapter numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; captioning automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering; captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic numbering;of objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter numbers in captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;chapter numbers in captions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147684				0	id	\<variable id=\"captions_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\"\>Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147395				0	id	You can include chapter numbers in captions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147408				0	id	Ensure that the text in your document is organized by chapters, and that the chapter titles and, if you want, the section titles, use one of the predefined heading paragraph styles. You must also assign a numbering option to the heading paragraph styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154249				0	id	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	id	Pilih \<emph\>Sisip - Seksi\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527	19			0	id	Select a caption title from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Category\</item\> box, and select a numbering style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> box. \<br/\>You also can enter a caption text in this dialog. If you want, enter text in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Caption\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Opsi\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> box, select the number of heading levels to include in the chapter number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553				0	id	Type the character that you want to separate the chapter number(s) from the caption number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Separator\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	id	In the \<emph\>Caption\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226				0	id	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, or table. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145567				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01041100.xhp\" name=\"Caption dialog\"\>AutoCaption dialog\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145574				0	id	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Chapter numbering\"\>Chapter numbering\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Outline Numbering				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147682				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>outlines;numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;heading numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headings; numbering/paragraph styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering;headings\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147682				0	id	\<variable id=\"chapter_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Outline Numbering\"\>Outline Numbering\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155605				0	id	You can modify the heading hierarchy or assign a level in the hierarchy to a custom paragraph style. You can also add chapter and section numbering to heading paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading 1" paragraph style is at the top of the outline hierarchy.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155626				0	id	To Add Automatic Numbering to a Heading Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155891				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paragraph Style\</item\> box, select the heading style that you want to add chapter numbers to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> box, select the numbering style that you want to use, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CE				0	id	To Remove Automatic Outline Numbering From a Heading Paragraph				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	id	Click at the beginning of the text in the heading paragraph, after the number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D9				0	id	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Backspace\</item\> key to delete the number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155552				0	id	To Use a Custom Paragraph Style as a Heading				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155571				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147758				0	id	Select the custom style in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147782	39			0	id	Click the heading level that you want to assign to the custom paragraph style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> list. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147808				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Defining Different Headers and Footers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155920				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>headers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining; headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mirrored page layout\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155920				0	id	\<variable id=\"header_pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Defining Different Headers and Footers\"\>Defining Different Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	id	You can use different headers and footers on different pages in your document, so long as the pages use different page styles. $[officename] provides several predefined page styles, such as \<emph\>First page\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left page\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right page\</emph\>, or you can create a custom page style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147105				0	id	You can also use the mirrored page layout if you want to add a header to a page style that has different inner and outer page margins. To apply this option to a page style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page\</item\> tab, and in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Layout settings\</item\> area, choose “Mirrored” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page layout\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	id	For example, you can use page styles to define different headers for even and odd pages in a document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150929				0	id	Open a new text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon in the Styles and Formatting window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	id	Right-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	id	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\> box, select "Left Page".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146889				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150714				0	id	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, right-click "Left Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150748				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	id	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147061				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\> box, select "Right Page".				20181231 09:50:43
