helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150537				0	id	\<variable id=\"captions\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Using Captions\"\>Using Captions\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153156				0	id	In text documents, you can add continuously numbered captions to graphics, tables, frames, and drawing objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	id	You can edit the text and the number ranges for different types of captions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153186				0	id	When you add a caption to a picture or to an object, the object and the caption text are placed together in a new frame. When you add a caption to a table, the caption text is inserted as a paragraph next to the table. When you add a caption to a frame, the caption text is added to the text inside the frame, either before or after the existing text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	id	To move both the object and the caption, drag the frame that contains these items. To update the caption numbering after you move the frame, press F9.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155541				0	id	To define a caption proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155567				0	id	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	id	Pilih \<emph\>Sisip - Seksi\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147765				0	id	Select the options that you want, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>. If you want, you can also enter different text in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Category\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Figure\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	id	You can edit caption text directly in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147271				0	id	A caption is formatted with the paragraph style that matches the name of the caption category. For example, if you insert a "Table" caption, the "Table" paragraph style is applied to the caption text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145671				0	id	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, frame, or table. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
