helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174				0	id	\<variable id=\"subscript\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/subscript.xhp\" name=\"Making Text Superscript or Subscript\"\>Making Text Superscript or Subscript\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	id	Select the text that you want to make superscript or subscript.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3155865				0	id	Lakukan satu dari langkah-langkah berikut:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character - Position\</emph\>, and then select \<emph\>Superscript\</emph\> or \<emph\>Subscript\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3156111				0	id	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+P to make the text superscript, and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+B to make the text subscript.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Character - Position\"\>Format - Character - Position\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect - Replace\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Replace\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145083				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; from Gallery into text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting from Gallery into text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;objects from Gallery\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145083				0	id	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop\"\>Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	id	You can drag-and-drop an object from the gallery into a text document, spreadsheet, drawing, or presentation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923				0	id	To replace a gallery object that you inserted in a document, hold down Shift+Ctrl, and then drag a different gallery object onto the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149637				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; removing/interrupting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullet lists; interrupting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;removing/interrupting numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>interrupting numbered lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;starting numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149637				0	id	\<variable id=\"numbering_paras\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_paras.xhp\" name=\"Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\"\>Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3145092				0	id	You can remove the numbering from a paragraph in a numbered list or change the number that a numbered list starts with.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id2172612				0	id	If you want numbered headings, use the \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> menu command to assign a numbering to a paragraph style. Do not use the Numbering icon on the Formatting toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145107				0	id	To Remove the Number From a Paragraph in a Numbered List				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3156248				0	id	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph that you want to remove the numbering from.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153366				0	id	Lakukan satu dari langkah-langkah berikut:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390				0	id	To remove the number while preserving the indent of the paragraph, press the Backspace key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	id	To remove the number and the indent of the paragraph, click the \<emph\>Numbering on/off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar. If you save the document in HTML format, a separate numbered list is created for the numbered paragraphs that follow the current paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154856				0	id	To Change the Number That a Numbered List Starts With				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155877				0	id	Click anywhere in the numbered list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3148691	22			0	id	Enter the number you want the list to start with in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Start \</item\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>at\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3147116				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id6943571				0	id	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Setting_up_a_Style_for_Numbering_Lines_in_Code_Listings\"\>Wiki page about numbering paragraphs by styles\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Conditional Text for Page Counts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153108				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>page counts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text;page counts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153108				0	id	\<variable id=\"conditional_text2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text2.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text for Page Counts\"\>Conditional Text for Page Counts\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156228				0	id	You can create a conditional text field that displays the word "pages" instead of "page" in conjunction with a page count field if your document contains more than one page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	id	Klik pada dokumen Anda di mana Anda hendak menyisipkan indeks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</item\>, and then enter a space.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	id	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256				0	id	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page > 1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145280				0	id	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Pages\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Then\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145305				0	id	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Else\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	id	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Word Completion for Text Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>automatic word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>completion of words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion;using/disabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>disabling;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>switching off;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deactivating;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>refusing word completions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rejecting word completions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	id	\<variable id=\"word_completion\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion.xhp\"\>Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076F				0	id	$[officename] collects words that you frequently use in the current session. When you later type the first three letters of a collected word, $[officename] automatically completes the word. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	91			0	id	If there is more than one word in the AutoCorrect memory that matches the three letters that you type, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to cycle through the available words. To cycle in the opposite direction, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Tab. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078D				0	id	 To Accept/Reject a Word Completion				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10794				0	id	By default, you accept the word completion by pressing the Enter key. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079B				0	id	 To reject the word completion, continue typing with any other key. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079E				0	id	 To Switch off the Word Completion 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A5				0	id	 Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Word Completion\</item\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AD				0	id	 Clear \<emph\>Enable word completion\</emph\> . 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id7504806				0	id	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion_adjust.xhp\"\>Fine-Tuning the Word Completion\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Conditional Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155619				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>matching conditional text in fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>if-then queries as fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text; setting up\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; conditional text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;conditions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155619				0	id	\<variable id=\"conditional_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text\"\>Conditional Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	id	You can set up fields in your document that display text when a condition that you define is met. For example, you can define the conditional text that is displayed in a series of reminder letters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	id	Setting up conditional text in this example is a two-part process. First you create a variable, and then you create the condition.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153175				0	id	To Define a Conditional Variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153185	62			0	id	The first part of the example is to define a variable for the condition statement. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155566				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variables\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759				0	id	Click "Set variable" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147784				0	id	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	id	Click "Text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id7748344				0	id	Enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.\<br/\>The Format list now displays a "General" format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645				0	id	To Define a Condition and the Conditional Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145659				0	id	The second part of the example is to define the condition that must be met, and to insert a placeholder for displaying the conditional text in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193				0	id	Place the cursor where you want to insert the conditional text in your text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	id	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	id	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder EQ "3"\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969				0	id	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150446				0	id	Type the text that you want to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box. There is almost no limit to the length of the text that you can enter. You can paste a paragraph into this box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150473				0	id	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155073				0	id	To Display the Conditional Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086				0	id	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110				0	id	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	id	Replace the number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box with 3, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168				0	id	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145714				0	id	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"Daftar operator\"\>Daftar operator\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode				20181231 09:50:43
