helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;protecting/unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unprotecting tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting;tables and sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id6007263				0	id	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</item\>\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id1924802				0	id	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150114				0	id	Protecting Sections in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	id	Any section of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text document can be protected against changes with a password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4545426				0	id	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the section against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	id	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	id	Select the text. Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section - Section\</emph\>, then under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> mark the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> and \<emph\>With password\</emph\> check boxes. (If the section already exists: \<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>.) Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	id	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147173				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - Sections - Section\</emph\> and under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> clear the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> check box. Enter the correct password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146081				0	id	Protecting Cells in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer Table				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	id	You can protect the contents of individual cells of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text table from changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id363170				0	id	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the cells against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	id	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	id	Place the cursor in a cell or select cells. Right-click to open the context menu, then choose \<emph\>Cell - Protect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	id	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	id	Place the cursor in the cell or select the cells. First, if necessary, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\> and mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>. Then right-click the cell to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Cell - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3151189				0	id	Select the table in the Navigator, open the context menu and select \<emph\>Table - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322				0	id	Use Shift+Ctrl+T to remove protection for the entire current table or all selected tables.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149259				0	id	Automatic Protection of Indexes and Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966				0	id	Tables of contents and indexes created automatically in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text are automatically protected against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id814539				0	id	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the contents against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145767				0	id	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153786				0	id	Place the cursor in the index/table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3159088				0	id	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, mark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118				0	id	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463	49			0	id	Place the cursor in the index. First of all, if necessary, under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids \</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152968				0	id	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, unmark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	id	In the Navigator, select the index, then open the context menu in the Navigator and select \<emph\>Index - Read-only\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
