helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	id	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Regular expressions\</item\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> box, type the search term and the wildcard(s) that you want to use in your search.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	id	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153401				0	id	Contoh Ekspresi Reguler				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	id	The wildcard for a single character is a period (.).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	id	The wildcard for zero or more occurrences of the previous character is an asterisk. For example: "123*" finds "12" "123", and "1233".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	id	The wildcard combination to search for zero or more occurrences of any character is a period and asterisk (.*).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149854				0	id	The wildcard for the end of a paragraph is a dollar sign ($). The wildcard character combination for the start of a paragraph is a caret and a period (^.).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200916345545				0	id	The wildcard for a tab character is \\t.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	id	A search using a regular expression will work only within one paragraph. To search using a regular expression in more than one paragraph, do a separate search in each paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"List of Wildcards\"\>List of Wildcards\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Emphasizing Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149820				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>text; emphasizing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>emphasizing text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820				0	id	\<variable id=\"text_emphasize\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_emphasize.xhp\" name=\"Emphasizing Text\"\>Emphasizing Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	id	Here are a few examples of how to emphasize text in a document:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	id	Select the text and apply a different font style or effect, such as \<emph\>bold\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149840	68			0	id	Right-click in a paragraph, choose \<emph\>Paragraph, \</emph\>set the options that you want, for example, the background color, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	id	Select the text, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Frame\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id6924649				0	id	Use the Text tool on the Drawing toolbar. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	id	Use Fontwork. To open the Fontwork window, click the Fontwork Gallery icon on the Drawing bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Nomor Halaman 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id5918759				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>page numbers;inserting/defining/formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles;page numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>starting page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;starting page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id413830				0	id	\<variable id=\"pagenumbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>Page Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1617175				0	id	In Writer, a page number is a field that you can insert into your text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id6091494				0	id	To Insert Page Numbers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id8611102				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\> to insert a page number at the current cursor position.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6604510				0	id	If you see the text "Page number" instead of the number, choose \<emph\>View - Field names\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2678914				0	id	However, these fields will change position when you add or remove text. So it is best to insert the page number field into a header or footer that has the same position and that is repeated on every page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id614642				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header - (name of page style)\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer - (name of page style)\</item\> to add a header or footer to all pages with the current page style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id2551652				0	id	To Start With a Defined Page Number				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6111941				0	id	Now you want some more control on page numbers. You are writing a text document that should start with page number 12.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5757621				0	id	Klik pada paragraf pertama dokumen Anda.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	id	PIlih \<emph\>Format - Halaman\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4395275				0	id	In the Breaks area, enable \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Enable \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\> just to be able to set the new \<emph\>Page number\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1654408				0	id	The new page number is an attribute of the first paragraph of the page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id7519150				0	id	To Format the Page Number Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9029206				0	id	You want roman page numbers running i, ii, iii, iv, and so on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3032319				0	id	Double-click directly before the page number field. You see the \<emph\>Edit Fields\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9139378				0	id	Select a number format and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5051728				0	id	Using Different Page Number Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1558885				0	id	You need some pages with the roman numbering style, followed by the remaining pages in another style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1541184				0	id	In Writer, you will need different page styles. The first page style has a footer with a page number field formatted for roman numbers. The following page style has a footer with a page number field formatted in another look.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id18616				0	id	Both page styles must be separated by a page break. In Writer, you can have automatic page breaks and manually inserted page breaks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	id	An \<emph\>automatic page break\</emph\> appears at the end of a page when the page style has a different "next style".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4569231				0	id	For example, the "First Page" page style has "Default" as the next style. To see this, you may press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon, right-click the First Page entry. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify\</item\> from the context menu. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab, you can see the "next style".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	id	A \<emph\>manually inserted page break\</emph\> can be applied without or with a change of page styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	id	If you just press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>, you apply a page break without a change of styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5947141				0	id	If you choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual break\</emph\>, you can insert a page break without or with a change of style or with a change of page number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	id	It depends on your document what is best: to use a manually inserted page break between page styles, or to use an automatic change. If you just need one title page with a different style than the other pages, you can use the automatic method:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	id	To Apply a Different Page Style to the First Page				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	id	Klik pada paragraf pertama dokumen Anda.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4313791				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	id	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	id	Double-click the "First Page" style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	id	Now your title page has the style "First Page", and the next pages automatically have the "Default" style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id399182				0	id	You can now for example insert a footer for the "Default" page atyle only, or insert footers in both page styles, but with differently formatted page number fields.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5298318				0	id	To Apply a Manually Inserted Page Style Change				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	id	Click at the start of the first paragraph on the page where a different page style will be applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>. You see the \<emph\>Insert Break\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> list box, select a page style. You may set a new page number, too. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	id	The selected page style will be used from the current paragraph to the next page break with style. You may need to create the new page style first.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	About Headers and Footers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	id	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	id	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	id	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	id	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119				0	id	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	id	You can also choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer\</item\> tab, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer on\</item\>. Clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Same content left/right\</item\> check box if you want to define different headers and footers for even and odd pages.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876				0	id	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704				0	id	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	34			0	id	Some of the header and footer options are also available for HTML documents. Headers and footers are not supported by HTML and instead are exported with special tags, so that they can be viewed in a browser. Headers and footers are only exported in HTML documents if they are enabled in Web Layout mode. When you reopen the document in $[officename], the headers and footers are displayed correctly, including any fields that you inserted. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	id	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Spacing Between Footnotes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147683				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>spacing; endnotes/footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>endnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders;for footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147683				0	id	\<variable id=\"footnote_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Spacing Between Footnotes\"\>Spacing Between Footnotes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3145808				0	id	If you want to increase the spacing between footnote or endnote texts, you can add a top and bottom border to the corresponding paragraph style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	id	Click in a footnote or endnote.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154251				0	id	Right-click the Paragraph Style that you want to modify, for example, "Footnote", and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155884				0	id	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Borders\"\>\<emph\>Borders\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Default\</item\> area, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Set Top and Bottom Borders Only\</item\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Line\</item\> area, click a line in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150961				0	id	Select "White" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Color\</item\> box. If the background of the page is not white, select the color that best matches the background color.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	id	In the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area, clear the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150709				0	id	Enter a value in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Top\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Bottom\</item\> boxes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Borders\"\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Indenting Paragraphs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155869				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>formatting; indenting paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>indents;in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; indents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hanging indents in paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right indents in paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines of text; indents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;indents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	hd_id129398				0	id	\<variable id=\"indenting\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indenting.xhp\"\>Indenting Paragraphs\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id5589159				0	id	To change the measurement units, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</item\>, and then select a new measurement unit in the Settings area. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id9936216				0	id	You can change the indents for the current paragraph, or for all selected paragraphs, or for a Paragraph Style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id7953123				0	id	You can also \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\" name=\"ruler\"\>set indents using the ruler\</link\>. To display the ruler, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Ruler\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</item\> to change the indents for the current paragraph or for all selected paragraphs. You can also \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\" name=\"ruler\"\>set indents using the ruler\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	id	Right-click a paragraph and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style - Indents & Spacing\</item\> to change the indents for all paragraphs that have the same Paragraph Style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id7271645				0	id	Indents are calculated with respect to the left and right page margins. If you want the paragraph to extend into the page margin, enter a negative number. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	id	The indents are different regarding the writing direction. For example, look at the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before text \</item\>indent value in left-to-right languages. The left edge of the paragraph is indented with respect to the left page margin. In right-to-left languages, the right edge of the paragraph is indented with respect to the right page margin.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	id	For a hanging indent, enter a positive value for \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before text\</item\> and a negative value for \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>First line\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\"\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Finding and Replacing in Writer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id1163670				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>finding; text/text formats/styles/objects\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>replacing; text and text formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>styles;finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>text formats; finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>formats; finding and replacing\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching; formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>objects;finding by Navigator\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Asian languages;search options\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8568681				0	id	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Writer\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id611285				0	id	In text documents you can find words, formatting, styles, and more. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all results at once, then apply another format or replace the words by other text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id6226081				0	id	The Find & Replace dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6702780				0	id	To find text within the whole document, open the Find & Replace dialog without any active text selection. If you want to search only a part of your document, first select that part of text, then open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158970				0	id	To Find Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6957304				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2164677				0	id	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5684072				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Cari\</emph\> atau \<emph\>Cari Semua\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4377269				0	id	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Writer will show you the next text that is equal to your entry. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found text. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1371807				0	id	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next text without opening the dialog. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id924100				0	id	Alternatively, you can use the icons at the lower right of the document to navigate to the next text or to any other object in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9359416				0	id	When you click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>, Writer selects all text that is equal to your entry. Now you can for example set all found text to bold, or apply a character style to all at once.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id5891598				0	id	To Replace Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1780755				0	id	Unlike searching text, replacing text cannot be restricted to the current selection only.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2467421				0	id	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4286935				0	id	Enter the text to search in the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9959410				0	id	Enter the text to replace the found text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id24109				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Cari\</emph\> atau \<emph\>Cari Semua\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id703451				0	id	When you click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>, Writer will search the whole document for the text in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, starting at the current cursor position. When text is found, Writer highlights the text and waits for your response. Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> to replace the highlighted text in the document with the text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box. Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> to advance to the next found text without replacing the current selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7540818				0	id	When you click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>, Writer replaces all text that matches your entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id9908444				0	id	To Find Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8413953				0	id	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain Paragraph Style is assigned, for example the "Heading 2" style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2696920				0	id	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id896938				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Pilihan Lebih\</emph\> untuk memperlebar dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9147007				0	id	Check \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for Styles\</item\>.\<br/\>The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> text box now is a list box, where you can select any of the Paragraph Styles that are applied in the current document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id679342				0	id	Select the style to search for, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3231299				0	id	To Find Formats				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8087405				0	id	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain direct character formatting is assigned. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3406170				0	id	Finding formats only finds direct character attributes, it does not find attributes applied as part of a style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2448805				0	id	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4542985				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Pilihan Lebih\</emph\> untuk memperlebar dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4679403				0	id	Klik tombol \<emph\>Format\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7783745				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Cari\</emph\> atau \<emph\>Cari Semua\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5597094				0	id	More options				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9919431				0	id	The similarity search can find text that is almost the same as your search text. You can set the number of characters that are allowed to differ.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8533280				0	id	Check the \<emph\>Similarity search\</emph\> option and optionally click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to change the settings. (Setting all three numbers to 1 works fine for English text.)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4646748				0	id	When you have enabled Asian language support under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>, the Find & Replace dialog offers options to search Asian text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2489394				0	id	The Navigator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9934385				0	id	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects. You can also use the Navigator to move and arrange chapters, providing an outline view to your document. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4159062				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7421796				0	id	Use the Navigator for inserting objects, links and references within the same document or from other open documents. See the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/navigator.xhp\"\>Navigator\</link\> guide for more information.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6417432				0	id	Click the icon with the blue circle at the bottom right part of your document to open the small \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4639728				0	id	Use the small Navigation window to quickly jump to the next object or find the next text in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Calculating in Text Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149909				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references;in Writer tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149909				0	id	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Text Documents\"\>Calculating in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	id	You can insert a calculation directly into a text document or into a text table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	id	Click in the document where you want to insert the calculation, and then press F2. If you are in a table cell, type an equals sign =.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155547				0	id	Type the calculation that you want to insert, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=10000/12\</item\>, and then press Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155565				0	id	You can also click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, and then choose a function for your formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id8316904				0	id	To reference cells in a Writer text table, enclose the cell address or the cell range in angle brackets. For example, to reference cell A1 from another cell, enter =<A1> into the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Using Smart Tags				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155622				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>options;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>disabling;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3563951				0	id	\<variable id=\"smarttags\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/smarttags.xhp\"\>Using Smart Tags\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id368358				0	id	Smart Tags provide additional information and functionality to specified words in a Writer document. The available features can be different for different Smart Tags extensions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id9298379				0	id	Installing Smart Tags				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	id	Smart Tags can be supplied as \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>extensions\</link\> to %PRODUCTNAME Writer. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id2508621				0	id	To install a Smart Tag, do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id3856013				0	id	Save the *.oxt extension file to your harddrive, then double-click the *.oxt file in your file manager. Alternatively, in %PRODUCTNAME choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> to open the Extension Manager, click Add and browse to the file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id7814264				0	id	Click a Smart Tag *.oxt file link on a web page and open the link with the default application. This requires a properly configured Web browser.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id8142338				0	id	Smart Tags Menu				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1917477				0	id	Any text in a Writer document can be marked with a Smart Tag, by default a magenta colored underline. You can change the color in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Appearance\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id192266				0	id	When you point to a Smart Tag, a tip help informs you to Ctrl-click to open the Smart Tags menu. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the marked text and open the context menu by Shift+F10.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1998962				0	id	In the Smart Tags menu you see the available actions that are defined for this Smart Tag. Choose an option from the menu. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Smart Tags Options\</item\> command opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page of Tools - Autocorrect Options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id2376476				0	id	To Enable and Disable Smart Tags				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id349131				0	id	When you have installed at least one Smart Tags extension, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Autocorrect Options\</item\>. Use this dialog to enable or disable Smart Tags and to manage the installed tags.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1216467				0	id	Text that is recognized as a Smart Tag is not checked by the automatic spellcheck.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Calculating Cell Totals in Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147400				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;sums in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>totals in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>table cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sums of table cell series\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147400				0	id	\<variable id=\"calculate_intable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Cell Totals in Tables\"\>Calculating the Sum of a Series of Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Table\</emph\>, and insert a table with one column and more than one row into a text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154203				0	id	Type a number in each cell of the column, but leave the last cell in the column empty.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	id	Place the cursor in the last cell of the column, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sum\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table Bar\</item\>.\<br/\>The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\> appears with the entry "=sum".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147775				0	id	Click in the first cell of the series you want to sum up, drag to the final cell, and then release.\<br/\>$[officename] inserts a formula for calculating the sum of the values in the current column.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150507	8			0	id	Press Enter, or click \<emph\>Apply\</emph\> in the Formula bar. \<br/\>The sum of the values in the current column is entered in the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150533				0	id	If you enter a different number anywhere in the column, the sum is updated as soon as you click in the last column cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	id	Similarly, you can also quickly calculate the sum of a row of numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Inserting Sections				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>sections; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents;inserting linked sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;linked sections, manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	id	\<variable id=\"section_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Sections\"\>Inserting Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	id	You can insert new sections, or links to sections in other documents into the current document. If you insert a section as a link, the content of the link changes when you modify the source document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	id	To Insert a New Section				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	id	Click in your document where you want to insert a new section, or select the text that you want to convert to a section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156103				0	id	If you select a text that occurs within a paragraph, the text is automatically converted into a new paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	id	Pilih \<emph\>Sisip - Seksi\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Section\</item\> box, type a name for the section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	id	Set the options for the section, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149635				0	id	To Insert a Section as a Link				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	id	Before you can insert a section as link, you must first create sections in the source document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	id	When you open a document that contains linked sections, $[officename] prompts you to update the contents of the sections. To manually update a link, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Links\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149860				0	id	You can also insert linked sections in HTML documents. When you view the page in a web browser, the content of the sections corresponds to the content of the sections at the time the HTML document was last saved.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145104				0	id	Klik pada dokumen Anda di mana Anda hendak menyisipkan indeks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	id	Pilih \<emph\>Sisip - Seksi\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Section\</item\> box, type a name for the section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\> area, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\> check box. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Under Windows, you can also select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>DDE\</item\> check box to automatically update the contents of the section when the section in the source document is changed.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154852				0	id	Click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File name\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155882				0	id	Locate the document containing the section that you want to link to, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149978				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Section\</item\> box, select the section that you want to insert.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150003				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Sisip\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Menyeleksi Tabel, Baris, dan Kolom				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	bm_id7693411				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>selecting;tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows;selecting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F0				0	id	\<variable id=\"table_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_select.xhp\"\>Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060E				0	id	You can select a table in a text document with a keyboard or with a mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	id	To select a table with the keyboard, move the cursor into the table, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A until all the cells are selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10633				0	id	To select a table with the mouse, move the mouse pointer to a position just above and left of the table. The mouse pointer becomes a diagonal arrow. Click to select the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	id	To select a row or column with the mouse, point to a position just left of the row or above the column. The mouse pointer becomes an arrow. Click to select the row or column.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145078				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>tab stops; inserting in lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering; changing the level of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;changing levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>levels;changing outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;changing levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowering outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rising outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;outline levels\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145078				0	id	\<variable id=\"insert_tab_innumbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_tab_innumbering.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists\"\>Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155909				0	id	To move a numbered or bulleted paragraph down one outline level, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press Tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	id	To move a numbered or bulleted paragraph up one outline level, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press Shift+Tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153403	8			0	id	To insert a tab between the number or bullet and the paragraph text, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155186				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; editing or deleting entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; editing or deleting entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;entries of indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;table/index entries\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155186				0	id	\<variable id=\"indices_delete\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_delete.xhp\" name=\"Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries\"\>Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	12			0	id	Index entries are inserted as fields into your document. To view fields in your document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View\</item\> and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Field Shadings\</item\> is selected. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155507				0	id	Place the cursor immediately in front of the index entry in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155526	16			0	id	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Index Entry\</emph\>, and do one of the following: 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3154238				0	id	To change the entry, enter different text in the \<emph\>Entry\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	id	To remove the entry, click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155893				0	id	To cycle through the index entries in your document, click the next or the previous arrows in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02160000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Index Entry dialog\"\>\<emph\>Edit Index Entry\</emph\> dialog\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Working with Master Documents and Subdocuments				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145246				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;master documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;creating/editing/exporting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>subdocuments;creating/editing/removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;subdocuments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>indexes; master documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145246				0	id	\<variable id=\"globaldoc_howtos\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/globaldoc_howtos.xhp\"\>Working with Master Documents and Subdocuments\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id1522873				0	id	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	id	To Create a Master Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	id	Lakukan satu dari langkah-langkah berikut:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	id	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Master Document\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	id	Open an existing document and choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create Master Document\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	id	If you are creating a new master document, the first entry in the Navigator should be a \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text\</item\> entry. Type an introduction or enter some text. This ensures that after having edited an existing style in the master document, you see the changed style when viewing the subdocuments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145114				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Navigator\</item\> for master documents (should open automatically, else press F5 to open), click and hold the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> icon, and do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	id	To insert an existing file as a subdocument, choose \<emph\>File\</emph\>, locate the file that you want to include, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145405				0	id	To create a new subdocument, choose \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, type a name for the file, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8550981				0	id	To insert some text between subdocuments, choose \<emph\>Text\</emph\>. Then type the text. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153382				0	id	Pilih \<emph\>Berkas - Cetak\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	id	To Edit a Master Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	id	Use the Navigator for rearranging and editing the subdocuments in a master document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	id	To open a subdocument for editing, double-click the name of the subdocument in the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155931				0	id	To remove a subdocument from the master document, right-click the subdocument in the Navigator list and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. The subdocument file is not deleted, only the entry in the Navigator is removed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148677				0	id	To add text to a master document, right-click an item in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Text\</emph\>. A text section is inserted before the selected item in the master document where you can type the text that you want. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149982				0	id	To reorder the subdocuments in a master document, drag a subdocument to a new location in the Navigator list. You can also select a subdocument in the list, and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move down\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move up\</item\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153022				0	id	To add an index, such as a table of contents, right-click in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	id	\<image id=\"img_id3148959\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20246.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148959\"\>Ikon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	id	To update an index in a master document, select the index in the Navigator, and then click the \<emph\>Update\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C40				0	id	When you insert an object like a frame or a picture into a master document, do not anchor the object "to page". Instead, set the anchor "to paragraph" on the \<emph\>Format - (Object type) - Type\</emph\> tab page, and then set the object's position relative to "Entire Page" in the \<emph\>Horizontal\</emph\> and \<emph\>Vertical\</emph\> list boxes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153656				0	id	To Start Each Subdocument on a New Page				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	id	Ensure that each subdocument starts with a heading that uses the same paragraph style, for example "Heading 1".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	id	In the master document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153907				0	id	Right-click "Heading 1" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	id	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Flow\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Breaks\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>, and then select “Page” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	id	If you want each subdocument to start on an odd page, select \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>, and select "Right page" in the box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145205				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	id	To Export a Master Document as a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Text Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150315				0	id	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Export\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148580				0	id	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> list, select a text document file format and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8371227				0	id	The subdocuments will be exported as sections. Use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Sections\</item\> to unprotect and remove sections, if you prefer a plain text document without sections.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	id	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Mencetak Brosur				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	bm_id6743064				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>printing; individual brochures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>booklet printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>brochures; printing individual\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F6				0	id	\<variable id=\"print_brochure\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/print_brochure.xhp\"\>Mencetak Brosur\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	id	You can print a Writer document as a brochure or a booklet. That is, Writer prints two pages on each side of the paper, so that when you fold the paper, you can read the document as a book.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DE				0	id	When you create a document that you want to print as a brochure, use portrait orientation for the pages. Writer applies the brochure layout when you print the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	id	Untuk Mencetak Brosur				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10621				0	id	Pilih \<emph\>Berkas - Cetak\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B6				0	id	In the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070E				0	id	In the properties dialog for your printer, set the paper orientation to landscape.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_id8947416				0	id	If your printer prints duplex, and because brochures always print in landscape mode, you should use the "duplex - short edge" setting in your printer setup dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10628				0	id	Return to \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, and click the \<emph\>Page Layout\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1062C				0	id	Select \<emph\>Brochure\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10740				0	id	For a printer that automatically prints on both sides of a page, specify to include "All pages".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	id	If %PRODUCTNAME prints the pages in the wrong order, open the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, select \<emph\>Print in reverse page order\</emph\>, and then print the document again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Checking Spelling and Grammar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149684				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; checking text documents manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>checking spelling;manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>grammar checker\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149684				0	id	\<variable id=\"spellcheck_dialog\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/spellcheck_dialog.xhp\" name=\"Checking Spelling and Grammar\"\>Checking Spelling and Grammar\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149814				0	id	You can manually check the spelling and grammar of a text selection or the entire document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id0525200902184476				0	id	To check the spelling and the grammar of a text, the appropriate dictionaries must be installed. For many languages three different dictionaries exist: a spellchecker, a hyphenation dictionary, and a thesaurus. Each dictionary covers one language only. Grammar checkers can be downloaded and installed as extensions. See the \<link href=\"https://extensions.openoffice.org/dictionary\"\>extensions web page\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149828				0	id	The spellcheck starts at the current cursor position, or at the beginning of the text selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	id	Click in the document, or select the text that you want to check.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Spelling and Grammar\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	id	When a possible spelling error is encountered, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Spellcheck\</item\> dialog opens and $[officename] offers some suggested corrections.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149861				0	id	Lakukan satu dari langkah-langkah berikut:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3145099				0	id	To accept a correction, click the suggestion, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	id	Edit the sentence in the upper text box, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	id	To add the unknown word to a user-defined dictionary, click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
