helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146856				0	id	Select any options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146872				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146896				0	id	If you want to use a different paragraph style as a table of contents entry, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Additional Styles\</item\> check box in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Create from\</item\> area, and then click the (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) button next to the check box. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Assign Styles\</item\> dialog, click the style in the list, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>>>\</item\> or the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\><<\</item\> button to define the outline level for the paragraph style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153148				0	id	Memperbaharui Daftar Isi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153161				0	id	Lakukan satu dari langkah-langkah berikut:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183				0	id	Right-click in the table of contents and choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147066				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - All Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149487				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; inserting/editing/linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text flow; from frame to frame\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;hiding text frames from printing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	id	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	id	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104				0	id	To Insert a Text Frame				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	id	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	id	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115				0	id	To Edit a Text Frame				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	id	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	id	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	id	To resize a text frame, click an edge of the frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	id	To Hide Text From Printing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	id	Any Writer text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	id	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	id	Pilih \<emph\>Format - Halaman - Halaman\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	id	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	id	To Link Text Frames				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	id	You can link Writer text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	id	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	87			0	id	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Frame\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link Frames\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3148968\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_chainframes.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148968\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	id	Click the frame that you want to link to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	id	You can only link frames if:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	id	The target frame is empty.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	id	The target frame is not linked to another frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	id	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	id	The source frame does not have a next link.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	id	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	id	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id5853144				0	id	The AutoSize feature is available only for the last frame in a chain of linked frames.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; editing/updating/deleting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; editing and deleting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	id	\<variable id=\"indices_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_edit.xhp\" name=\"Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\"\>Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	id	Place the cursor in the index or table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155871				0	id	If you cannot place your cursor in the index or table of contents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</item\>, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Enable\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Cursor in protected areas\</item\> section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	id	Right-click and choose an editing option from the menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	id	You can also make changes directly to an index or table of contents. Right-click in the index or table of contents, choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Protected from manual changes\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	tit				0	id	Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155855				0	id	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing; index format\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>entries; in tables of contents, as hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; hyperlinks as entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; in tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;indexes and tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155855				0	id	\<variable id=\"indices_form\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_form.xhp\" name=\"Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\"\>Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3154259				0	id	You can apply different paragraph styles, assign hyperlinks to entries, change the layout of indexes, and change the background color of indexes in the \<emph\>Insert Index\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155888				0	id	To Apply a Different Paragraph Style to an Index Level				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	id	Right-click in the index or table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147135	46			0	id	Klik tabulasi \<emph\>Ganti\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150229	47			0	id	Click an index level in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934	48			0	id	Click the style that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960				0	id	Click the assign button \<emph\><\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150516				0	id	Klik \<emph\>Oke\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146878				0	id	To Assign Hyperlinks to Entries in a Table of Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3146890				0	id	You can assign a cross-reference as a hyperlink to entries in a table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150712				0	id	Right-click in the table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150738				0	id	Klik tabulasi \<emph\>Opsi\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148399				0	id	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> list click the heading level that you want to assign hyperlinks to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148424	53			0	id	In the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>area, click in the box in front of \<emph\>E#\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3153171				0	id	Click in the box behind the \<emph\>E\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147060				0	id	Repeat for each heading level that you want to create hyperlinks for, or click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>All\</item\> button to apply the formatting to all levels.				20181231 09:50:43
