helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	id	In Writer, you can define borders around OLE objects, plug-ins, diagrams/charts, graphics and frames. The name of the menu to be used depends on the object selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673				0	id	To Set a Predefined Border Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	id	Select the object for which you want to define a border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	4			0	id	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	id	Click one of the predefined border styles. This replaces the current border style of the object with the selected style.				20181231 09:50:43
