helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934				0	id	Outline numbering is linked to paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading" paragraph styles (1-10) are assigned to the corresponding outline number levels (1-10). If you want, you can assign different paragraph styles to the outline number level.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id8237250				0	id	If you want numbered headings, use the \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> menu command to assign numbering to a paragraph style. Do not use the Numbering icon on the Formatting toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147567	55			0	id	To highlight the screen display of outline numbers, choose \<emph\>View -\</emph\>\<emph\>Field Shadings\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151168				0	id	Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147512				0	id	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OUTLINE_FORM\"\>Saves or loads an outline number format. A saved outline number format is available to all text documents.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150979				0	id	The \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button is only available for outline numbering. For numbered or bulleted list styles, modify the Numbering Styles of the paragraphs.				20181231 09:50:43
