helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148572				0	id	\<variable id=\"silben\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts hyphens in words that are too long to fit at the end of a line.\</ahelp\> $[officename] searches the document and suggests hyphenation that you can accept or reject. If text is selected, the Hyphenation dialog works on the selected text only. If no text is selected, the Hyphenation dialog works on the whole document.\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	id	To automatically hyphenate the current or selected paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\> tab. You can also apply automatic hyphenation to a paragraph style. In text where automatic hyphenation is enabled, the Hyphenation dialog will not find any word to hyphenate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	id	Saat $[officename] menemukan sebuah kata yang perlu dipenggal, lakukan satu dari pilihan berikut:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155622				0	id	To accept the hyphenation of the displayed word, click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558				0	id	To change the hyphenation of the displayed word, click the left or right arrow below the word, and then click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>. The left and right buttons are enabled for words with multiple hyphenation points.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150017				0	id	To reject the hyphenation of the displayed word, click \<emph\>Skip\</emph\>. This word will not be hyphenated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150018				0	id	To automatically hyphenate the remaining part of the selection or the document, click \<emph\>Hyphenate All\</emph\> and answer "Yes" to the following question.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150019				0	id	To end hyphenation, click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>. The hyphenation that is applied already will not be reverted. You can use \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\> to undo all hyphenation that was applied while the Hyphenation dialog was open.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147562				0	id	To exclude paragraphs from the automatic hyphenation, select the paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, click the Text Flow tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box in the Hyphenation area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154276				0	id	To disable the Hyphenation dialog and always hyphenate automatically, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010400.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Writing Aids\"\>Language Settings - Writing Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and select the \<emph\>Hyphenate without inquiry\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152950				0	id	To manually enter a hyphen directly in the document, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Minus sign (-).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147523				0	id	To insert a non-breaking (protected) hyphen directly in the document, click in the word that you want to hyphenate, and then press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Minus sign(-).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573				0	id	To hide custom hyphens, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and then clear the \<emph\>Custom hyphens\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150360				0	id	Kata				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153676				0	id	Kata				20181231 09:50:43
